1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
<font color="#00FF00">{\an8}Downloaded from MoviesMod.at</font>

2
00:01:00,199 --> 00:01:02,159
<i>In the next five days...</i>

3
00:01:02,618 --> 00:01:04,412
<i>Muzan will come.</i>

4
00:01:10,793 --> 00:01:13,337
<i>Use me as bait...</i>

5
00:01:14,255 --> 00:01:17,049
<i>and cut off Muzan's head.</i>

6
00:01:20,803 --> 00:01:24,765
<i>What makes you think that?</i>

7
00:01:27,685 --> 00:01:29,019
<i>Just my intuition.</i>

8
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:30,563
<i>That's all.</i>

9
00:01:31,188 --> 00:01:32,940
<i>No reason.</i>

10
00:01:33,482 --> 00:01:36,903
<i>The other children... won't agree...</i>

11
00:01:37,028 --> 00:01:43,910
<i>to using me as bait.</i>

12
00:01:44,785 --> 00:01:47,704
<i>You're the only one that I can ask...</i>

13
00:01:47,705 --> 00:01:49,290
<i>Gyomei.</i>

14
00:01:51,334 --> 00:01:54,670
<i>Even if you behead him, he won't die.</i>

15
00:01:56,756 --> 00:01:59,800
<i>The only thing that can destroy Muzan...</i>

16
00:02:00,259 --> 00:02:03,930
<i>is most likely sunlight.</i>

17
00:02:04,931 --> 00:02:07,724
<i>If he doesn't die even after
you've destroyed his head...</i>

18
00:02:07,725 --> 00:02:10,144
<i>you'll be in...</i>

19
00:02:10,728 --> 00:02:14,357
<i>for a drawn-out battle
until the sun rises.</i>

20
00:02:15,816 --> 00:02:16,943
<i>Understood.</i>

21
00:02:18,444 --> 00:02:21,405
<i>If that is your wish, Master.</i>

22
00:02:24,825 --> 00:02:26,369
<i>Thank you.</i>

23
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:33,626
<i>Please...</i>

24
00:02:34,001 --> 00:02:35,962
<i>don't let any more...</i>

25
00:02:36,295 --> 00:02:39,340
<i>of my precious children die.</i>

26
00:02:39,715 --> 00:02:42,677
<i>That is my wish.</i>

27
00:03:00,861 --> 00:03:04,448
So, you think you've
driven me into a corner?

28
00:03:06,242 --> 00:03:09,661
You're all about to go straight to Hell!

29
00:03:09,662 --> 00:03:11,997
You eyesore Demon Slayers!

30
00:03:11,998 --> 00:03:14,917
Tonight, I'm going to massacre
every one of you!

31
00:03:19,964 --> 00:03:22,425
You're the one who's going to Hell, Muzan!

32
00:03:22,758 --> 00:03:24,593
You're not getting away, no matter what!

33
00:03:25,511 --> 00:03:27,387
Do it, then!

34
00:03:27,388 --> 00:03:29,432
Let's see you try...

35
00:03:29,807 --> 00:03:32,101
Tanjiro Kamado!

36
00:03:34,687 --> 00:03:36,397
I'll absolutely defeat you...

37
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:40,526
Muzan Kibutsuji!

38
00:03:52,079 --> 00:03:53,247
<i>What is this place?</i>

39
00:03:54,498 --> 00:03:56,834
<i>Horizontally, vertically,
it's all messed up!</i>

40
00:03:57,668 --> 00:03:59,627
KILL
<i>Was it built...</i>

41
00:03:59,628 --> 00:04:01,422
<i>with an enemy's Blood Demon Art?</i>

42
00:04:04,175 --> 00:04:06,427
<i>I don't know
what's going on around me...</i>

43
00:04:06,761 --> 00:04:09,180
<i>but I know Ms. Tamayo
was holding Muzan down!</i>

44
00:04:10,556 --> 00:04:11,557
<i>But...</i>

45
00:04:12,099 --> 00:04:13,893
<i>who knows how long she can last?</i>

46
00:04:16,645 --> 00:04:18,314
Calm down, Kanroji!

47
00:04:18,981 --> 00:04:20,316
R-Right!

48
00:04:20,691 --> 00:04:21,817
Stay with me!

49
00:05:16,956 --> 00:05:20,251
<i>I've got to reach Muzan
as soon as possible and defeat him!</i>

50
00:05:21,252 --> 00:05:22,670
<i>As soon as possible!</i>

51
00:05:30,928 --> 00:05:31,971
<i>That's the bottom!</i>

52
00:05:32,638 --> 00:05:34,473
<i>I'll be killed if I smash into it!</i>

53
00:05:34,849 --> 00:05:38,977
<i>I'll use a move to change my trajectory
and find something to grab onto!</i>

54
00:05:38,978 --> 00:05:40,271
{\an8}DESTROY

55
00:05:42,565 --> 00:05:43,898
<i>I'm off-balance!</i>

56
00:05:43,899 --> 00:05:47,236
<i>The pressure of the fall
is keeping me from exerting myself!</i>

57
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:50,531
{\an8}DESTROYER
OF DEMONS

58
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,928
Mr. Gi--

59
00:06:35,868 --> 00:06:37,077
Are you all right?

60
00:06:38,954 --> 00:06:39,954
Yes!

61
00:06:39,955 --> 00:06:41,540
Thank you very much!

62
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:44,585
You saved me--

63
00:06:46,712 --> 00:06:47,795
<i>Water Breathing...</i>

64
00:06:47,796 --> 00:06:49,048
<i>First Form...</i>

65
00:06:49,423 --> 00:06:51,258
<i>Water Surface Slash!</i>

66
00:06:53,135 --> 00:06:54,178
Tanjiro!

67
00:07:16,450 --> 00:07:17,868
<i>- Water Breathing...
- Water Breathing...</i>

68
00:07:18,327 --> 00:07:19,619
<i>Sixth Form...</i>

69
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:20,871
<i>Third Form...</i>

70
00:07:22,831 --> 00:07:24,374
<i>Whirlpool!</i>

71
00:07:24,375 --> 00:07:25,876
<i>Flowing Dance!</i>

72
00:07:33,842 --> 00:07:36,178
<i>Mr. Giyu's too amazing.</i>

73
00:07:36,553 --> 00:07:39,555
<i>He can tell from my slightest movement
which move I'm going to use.</i>

74
00:07:39,556 --> 00:07:44,061
<i>Then he unleashes his own in a way
that keeps us from slashing each other.</i>

75
00:07:44,395 --> 00:07:46,438
<i>He's unbelievable!</i>

76
00:07:46,855 --> 00:07:49,024
<i>What's going on in his mind right now?</i>

77
00:07:51,777 --> 00:07:53,112
This must be...

78
00:07:53,612 --> 00:07:57,449
that demon base Shinazugawa
and Iguro mentioned.

79
00:08:00,619 --> 00:08:01,953
Meaning that...

80
00:08:01,954 --> 00:08:05,039
Kibutsuji must've gathered us all here...

81
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:08,043
to wipe out the Hashira
and the Demon Slayer Corps.

82
00:08:09,461 --> 00:08:13,590
From here on in,
we'll need to be even more vigilant.

83
00:08:14,133 --> 00:08:15,467
Right!

84
00:08:17,136 --> 00:08:18,846
- Let's go.
- Right!

85
00:08:41,452 --> 00:08:42,702
<i>Serpent Breathing...</i>

86
00:08:42,703 --> 00:08:44,121
<i>Fifth Form...</i>

87
00:08:51,337 --> 00:08:53,130
<i>Slithering Serpent!</i>

88
00:08:56,050 --> 00:08:58,177
Stay away from Kanroji...

89
00:08:58,594 --> 00:08:59,803
you scums!

90
00:09:01,638 --> 00:09:03,932
<i>Mr. Iguro, you're so wonderful!</i>

91
00:09:05,059 --> 00:09:07,101
- Are you hurt?
- Not at all!

92
00:09:07,102 --> 00:09:08,896
- Come on, then.
- Right!

93
00:09:29,583 --> 00:09:30,626
Tokito!

94
00:09:37,925 --> 00:09:40,259
That's a huge horde of demons.

95
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:43,555
Looks like they've been given
Lower Rank-level powers.

96
00:09:43,931 --> 00:09:47,309
They're being used to try
and wear us down.

97
00:09:52,981 --> 00:09:54,691
What about the Master?

98
00:09:55,317 --> 00:09:57,611
He went on ahead of us.

99
00:09:58,779 --> 00:10:01,073
It was a noble end.

100
00:10:02,449 --> 00:10:03,659
The Master...

101
00:10:04,076 --> 00:10:07,913
would never make a mistake
like allowing a demon to find him.

102
00:10:08,288 --> 00:10:09,957
Did he use himself as bait?

103
00:10:10,958 --> 00:10:12,126
That's right.

104
00:10:12,584 --> 00:10:15,671
Because he didn't
have much longer to live.

105
00:10:22,052 --> 00:10:23,512
Master...

106
00:10:30,477 --> 00:10:32,228
When I was hovering...

107
00:10:32,229 --> 00:10:34,313
between life and death...

108
00:10:34,314 --> 00:10:36,525
after a demon attack...

109
00:10:37,526 --> 00:10:39,820
the Master was there for me
the whole time.

110
00:10:41,989 --> 00:10:44,408
He did the same for every Corps member...

111
00:10:44,741 --> 00:10:46,785
in their final moments.

112
00:10:48,954 --> 00:10:50,664
Like a father.

113
00:10:52,624 --> 00:10:55,002
Yes. I know.

114
00:10:55,836 --> 00:10:58,045
Muzan not only took my brother from me...

115
00:10:58,046 --> 00:11:00,507
but our father, as well.

116
00:11:01,383 --> 00:11:02,593
Damn him...

117
00:11:02,926 --> 00:11:04,011
Muzan!

118
00:11:04,636 --> 00:11:06,929
I'm going to torture him to death!

119
00:11:06,930 --> 00:11:09,308
I'll show him what Hell looks like!

120
00:11:09,933 --> 00:11:11,435
Don't worry.

121
00:11:16,064 --> 00:11:19,109
We all feel the same way.

122
00:11:25,991 --> 00:11:27,493
<i>Master...</i>

123
00:11:29,995 --> 00:11:31,747
<i>I couldn't protect you.</i>

124
00:11:47,429 --> 00:11:50,557
There's no end to you lowlifes.

125
00:11:53,810 --> 00:11:55,895
Show me what you've got!

126
00:11:55,896 --> 00:11:58,649
I'll kill every last one of you!

127
00:12:07,741 --> 00:12:08,909
Comin'...

128
00:12:09,284 --> 00:12:10,619
through!

129
00:12:13,664 --> 00:12:15,916
More falling, huh?

130
00:12:17,417 --> 00:12:20,504
I ended up in this crazy place
without any warning...

131
00:12:21,088 --> 00:12:24,675
but there's a whole boatload of demons,
so it's the perfect place...

132
00:12:25,509 --> 00:12:27,719
to test the results of my training!

133
00:12:38,021 --> 00:12:39,689
<i>What is this place?</i>

134
00:12:39,690 --> 00:12:42,234
<i>Is it the demon headquarters?
Where are the others?</i>

135
00:12:43,026 --> 00:12:44,236
<i>Big Brother...</i>

136
00:12:45,487 --> 00:12:47,739
<i>Please be safe, too, Big Brother!</i>

137
00:12:52,494 --> 00:12:54,204
<i>I just heard a sound.</i>

138
00:12:54,871 --> 00:12:56,957
<i>He might be somewhere nearby!</i>

139
00:13:02,671 --> 00:13:04,548
I'll never forgive him!

140
00:13:05,924 --> 00:13:07,050
No way...

141
00:13:07,342 --> 00:13:09,553
am I ever going to forgive him!

142
00:13:33,994 --> 00:13:35,996
<i>It smells like blood.</i>

143
00:13:44,755 --> 00:13:46,340
<i>What is this place?</i>

144
00:14:05,609 --> 00:14:07,778
Oh my, is someone here?

145
00:14:08,612 --> 00:14:10,989
Wow, and you're a girl!

146
00:14:11,865 --> 00:14:15,243
You look so young and tasty!

147
00:14:16,078 --> 00:14:19,956
I'll have to thank Nakime for this later.

148
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:36,640
<i>Shinobu...</i>

149
00:14:38,016 --> 00:14:40,352
<i>Leave the Demon Slayer Corps.</i>

150
00:14:41,895 --> 00:14:44,856
<i>I know you're trying hard.</i>

151
00:14:45,273 --> 00:14:48,026
<i>You're really giving it your all...</i>

152
00:14:48,902 --> 00:14:51,780
<i>but Shinobu, you'll probably...</i>

153
00:14:57,035 --> 00:15:00,872
<i>I want you to be happy
like any normal girl...</i>

154
00:15:01,623 --> 00:15:04,710
<i>and live on until you're elderly.</i>

155
00:15:06,712 --> 00:15:07,838
<i>You've already...</i>

156
00:15:08,213 --> 00:15:09,547
<i>done enough.</i>

157
00:15:09,548 --> 00:15:10,756
<i>No!</i>

158
00:15:10,757 --> 00:15:12,425
<i>No way am I quitting!</i>

159
00:15:12,426 --> 00:15:15,052
<i>I'm going to avenge you
if it's the last thing I do!</i>

160
00:15:15,053 --> 00:15:16,470
<i>Tell me!</i>

161
00:15:16,471 --> 00:15:17,805
<i>What did the demon look like?</i>

162
00:15:17,806 --> 00:15:20,142
<i>Which bastard got you?</i>

163
00:15:20,517 --> 00:15:22,518
<i>Tell me, Big Sister!</i>

164
00:15:22,519 --> 00:15:24,478
<i>Please!</i>

165
00:15:24,479 --> 00:15:28,692
<i>I could never live a normal life
after someone did this to you!</i>

166
00:15:29,192 --> 00:15:30,527
<i>Big Sister!</i>

167
00:15:34,990 --> 00:15:36,533
<i>It was a demon...</i>

168
00:15:36,908 --> 00:15:39,786
<i>who looked like he had
blood poured on his head.</i>

169
00:15:41,329 --> 00:15:42,664
Well, well...

170
00:15:42,998 --> 00:15:44,499
nice to meet you!

171
00:15:44,833 --> 00:15:47,210
My name is Doma.

172
00:15:47,669 --> 00:15:51,047
What a wonderful night.

173
00:15:52,257 --> 00:15:55,051
<i>With a carefree smile on his face...</i>

174
00:15:55,844 --> 00:15:59,556
<i>he speaks in a serene, gentle manner.</i>

175
00:16:01,433 --> 00:16:03,851
H-Help me...

176
00:16:03,852 --> 00:16:04,936
Please help me!

177
00:16:05,437 --> 00:16:07,146
Shh!

178
00:16:07,147 --> 00:16:09,024
Can't you see that I'm talking?

179
00:16:14,237 --> 00:16:15,947
Are you okay?

180
00:16:16,323 --> 00:16:18,616
Wow! You're fast!

181
00:16:18,617 --> 00:16:20,410
Are you a Hashira?

182
00:16:29,127 --> 00:16:30,878
Oh, don't worry!

183
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:33,172
You can just leave her there.

184
00:16:33,173 --> 00:16:35,633
I'll be sure to eat her later.

185
00:16:35,634 --> 00:16:36,968
Upsy-daisy.

186
00:16:38,762 --> 00:16:40,013
<i>The weapons...</i>

187
00:16:40,722 --> 00:16:42,390
<i>that demon wielded...</i>

188
00:16:42,974 --> 00:16:45,644
<i>were a pair of sharp fans.</i>

189
00:16:48,522 --> 00:16:52,442
I'm the founder
of the Eternal Paradise Faith.

190
00:16:52,818 --> 00:16:56,321
My job is to attain bliss
with all of my worshippers.

191
00:16:56,738 --> 00:16:59,616
So, I'll be sure to pick
that girl clean, too.

192
00:17:00,909 --> 00:17:02,660
<i>This guy...</i>

193
00:17:02,661 --> 00:17:05,497
<i>is the demon who killed my big sister.</i>

194
00:17:06,581 --> 00:17:08,582
Everyone's bliss?

195
00:17:08,583 --> 00:17:10,252
How deluded are you?

196
00:17:10,669 --> 00:17:14,046
This girl was unwilling
and crying out for help.

197
00:17:14,047 --> 00:17:16,550
And isn't that why I saved her?

198
00:17:16,842 --> 00:17:19,760
That girl's no longer suffering.

199
00:17:19,761 --> 00:17:23,306
She's no longer in pain
and no longer in fear.

200
00:17:23,890 --> 00:17:26,725
Everyone's afraid of death, you know.

201
00:17:26,726 --> 00:17:29,603
So, I do them a favor by eating them.

202
00:17:29,604 --> 00:17:32,189
They get to live on with me.

203
00:17:32,190 --> 00:17:34,317
For all eternity!

204
00:17:34,901 --> 00:17:37,194
To save my followers,
I take in their desires,

205
00:17:37,195 --> 00:17:39,363
their blood and their flesh...

206
00:17:39,364 --> 00:17:42,116
and guide them...

207
00:17:42,117 --> 00:17:45,119
to ever greater heights.

208
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:48,122
You can't possibly be in your right mind.

209
00:17:48,123 --> 00:17:50,416
Are you sure you're mentally intact?

210
00:17:50,417 --> 00:17:52,460
You truly make me want to gag!

211
00:17:52,961 --> 00:17:54,462
What?

212
00:17:55,213 --> 00:17:58,883
We've only just met,
but you're being awfully hostile.

213
00:17:58,884 --> 00:18:00,468
Oh! I see.

214
00:18:00,969 --> 00:18:02,761
You poor thing.

215
00:18:02,762 --> 00:18:05,473
You must've gone through
something unbearable.

216
00:18:05,765 --> 00:18:07,224
I'd be happy to listen.

217
00:18:07,225 --> 00:18:09,019
Go on, let it all out.

218
00:18:10,312 --> 00:18:13,230
"Unbearable" barely even scratches
the surface!

219
00:18:13,231 --> 00:18:16,483
The one who killed my big sister,
it was you!

220
00:18:16,484 --> 00:18:19,279
Doesn't this haori ring a bell?

221
00:18:19,696 --> 00:18:20,989
Huh?

222
00:18:32,834 --> 00:18:34,043
Oh!

223
00:18:34,044 --> 00:18:37,172
You mean that girl
who used Flower Breathing?

224
00:18:37,589 --> 00:18:40,383
Such a gentle, sweet child!

225
00:18:40,842 --> 00:18:43,677
The one I didn't get to devour
because the sun came up.

226
00:18:43,678 --> 00:18:45,013
I remember her.

227
00:18:45,305 --> 00:18:47,891
I sure wish I could've eaten her--

228
00:18:49,851 --> 00:18:51,226
<i>Insect Breathing...</i>

229
00:18:51,227 --> 00:18:52,937
<i>Dance of the Bee Sting...</i>

230
00:18:52,938 --> 00:18:54,230
<i>True Flutter!</i>

231
00:18:55,231 --> 00:18:58,652
What an astounding thrust!
I couldn't stop it with my hand!

232
00:19:00,737 --> 00:19:01,738
<i>Blood Demon Art...</i>

233
00:19:03,907 --> 00:19:06,117
<i>Frozen Lotus.</i>

234
00:19:06,952 --> 00:19:10,538
<i>It's freezing! The air's so cold,
it feels like it's ripping my lungs apart!</i>

235
00:19:11,748 --> 00:19:14,876
Oh, you sure are a quick one!

236
00:19:15,627 --> 00:19:17,795
But too bad for you.

237
00:19:17,796 --> 00:19:20,882
Thrusts can't kill a demon.

238
00:19:24,427 --> 00:19:25,845
It's the neck.

239
00:19:26,221 --> 00:19:28,681
You need to chop off the head.

240
00:19:28,682 --> 00:19:30,809
{\an8}DESTROY

241
00:19:31,184 --> 00:19:33,561
I may not be able
to kill you with my thrusts...

242
00:19:33,937 --> 00:19:35,313
but what about poison?

243
00:19:40,193 --> 00:19:44,489
<i>I'll find out now whether this poison
will work on an Upper Rank.</i>

244
00:19:45,490 --> 00:19:46,616
<i>Big Sister...</i>

245
00:19:47,283 --> 00:19:48,326
<i>please!</i>

246
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:50,036
<i>Big Sister!</i>

247
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:53,999
This is...

248
00:19:54,332 --> 00:19:57,126
stronger than the poison you used...

249
00:19:57,127 --> 00:19:59,546
on Rui's mountain, isn't it?

250
00:20:00,630 --> 00:20:03,757
<i>So, they did exchange information
after all.</i>

251
00:20:03,758 --> 00:20:05,759
<i>Poison is a double-edged sword.</i>

252
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:09,513
You... have been changing
the concoction for each demon!

253
00:20:09,514 --> 00:20:13,143
That's what he told me!

254
00:20:20,483 --> 00:20:22,443
What's this?

255
00:20:22,444 --> 00:20:26,447
Looks like I've neutralized your poison!

256
00:20:26,448 --> 00:20:27,823
Sorry about that!

257
00:20:27,824 --> 00:20:31,161
Even though you used it just for me!

258
00:20:32,328 --> 00:20:33,663
That sword...

259
00:20:34,164 --> 00:20:37,417
The sound it makes
when you sheathe it is unique.

260
00:20:38,209 --> 00:20:41,546
Is that where you change up the poison?

261
00:20:41,838 --> 00:20:44,299
Wow, this is fun!

262
00:20:45,425 --> 00:20:48,010
Getting poisoned is so amusing!

263
00:20:48,011 --> 00:20:49,929
It's almost addictive!

264
00:20:50,221 --> 00:20:52,639
Do you think your
next blend will work?

265
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:54,601
Let's give it a try!

266
00:21:01,024 --> 00:21:02,692
Very well.

267
00:21:03,276 --> 00:21:04,818
Fine by me.

268
00:21:04,819 --> 00:21:05,987
After all...

269
00:21:09,532 --> 00:21:12,619
I'd already anticipated
that this'd happen.

270
00:21:14,370 --> 00:21:16,288
Are you done mixing your new poison?

271
00:21:16,289 --> 00:21:19,000
I'm ready whenever you are!

272
00:21:22,670 --> 00:21:25,215
I know I told you to give it a try...

273
00:21:27,092 --> 00:21:30,261
but repeating the same strike
feels monotonous.

274
00:21:45,151 --> 00:21:48,655
What's this? You're slower than before.

275
00:21:49,197 --> 00:21:50,281
At this rate...

276
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:53,284
<i>Insect Breathing, Dance of the Horsefly...</i>

277
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:55,662
<i>Enticing Slash!</i>

278
00:22:03,545 --> 00:22:06,588
Whoops, you got a piece of me there, huh?

279
00:22:06,589 --> 00:22:09,424
You must have redirected
my counterattacks.

280
00:22:09,425 --> 00:22:12,428
That's amazing! I'm truly impressed!

281
00:22:12,804 --> 00:22:15,431
It's the touching fruits of your labor!

282
00:22:15,723 --> 00:22:17,933
You can keep piling it on!

283
00:22:17,934 --> 00:22:21,645
Why don't you launch your next attack
before I neutralize the poison?

284
00:22:21,646 --> 00:22:22,855
I can't help...

285
00:22:22,856 --> 00:22:26,192
wanting to cheer on people who try hard!

286
00:22:32,448 --> 00:22:33,448
Yes!

287
00:22:33,449 --> 00:22:34,617
That's the spirit!

288
00:22:37,871 --> 00:22:42,250
<i>Ever since I was a child,
I was kindhearted and smart.</i>

289
00:22:42,959 --> 00:22:48,422
<i>I never failed to help the pitiful,
and I made them happy.</i>

290
00:22:48,423 --> 00:22:50,925
<i>Because that was my duty.</i>

291
00:22:52,135 --> 00:22:55,430
<i>There are rainbows in this child's eyes.</i>

292
00:22:55,930 --> 00:22:59,559
<i>This pale gray hair
is proof of his innocence.</i>

293
00:23:00,143 --> 00:23:02,312
<i>This child is special.</i>

294
00:23:02,729 --> 00:23:05,565
<i>I'm sure that he can hear
the voices of the gods.</i>

295
00:23:07,358 --> 00:23:11,070
<i>My parents were hopelessly obtuse.</i>

296
00:23:11,738 --> 00:23:14,281
<i>Not that they could've
founded a stupid religion</i>

297
00:23:14,282 --> 00:23:17,368
<i>like the Eternal Paradise Faith otherwise.</i>

298
00:23:17,869 --> 00:23:19,704
<i>I felt sorry for them...</i>

299
00:23:20,079 --> 00:23:22,999
<i>so I always played along.</i>

300
00:23:24,292 --> 00:23:27,503
<i>I never once heard the voices of the gods.</i>

301
00:23:28,171 --> 00:23:30,881
<i>At first, I didn't know how
to deal with the hordes of people</i>

302
00:23:30,882 --> 00:23:34,761
<i>worshipping me and praying to me.</i>

303
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:37,971
<i>Seeing these grown-ups
come crying to a child like me...</i>

304
00:23:37,972 --> 00:23:41,725
<i>saying, "I'm suffering,
I'm in pain, what should I do?"...</i>

305
00:23:41,726 --> 00:23:44,812
<i>made me worry
whether their heads were okay.</i>

306
00:23:46,022 --> 00:23:49,275
<i>After nearly putting me to sleep
with their personal stories...</i>

307
00:23:49,817 --> 00:23:54,155
<i>they would bow down to me,
asking me to guide them to Paradise.</i>

308
00:23:54,739 --> 00:23:56,658
<i>I cried.</i>

309
00:23:57,242 --> 00:23:58,826
<i>You poor things.</i>

310
00:23:59,410 --> 00:24:02,121
<i>Paradise doesn't even exist.</i>

311
00:24:02,830 --> 00:24:06,668
<i>It's just a fairy tale
concocted by deluded humans.</i>

312
00:24:07,919 --> 00:24:10,338
<i>There are no gods nor buddhas.</i>

313
00:24:10,922 --> 00:24:16,719
<i>These people had lived for decades,
yet they still couldn't grasp that.</i>

314
00:24:17,303 --> 00:24:19,347
<i>When you die, you just become nothing.</i>

315
00:24:19,931 --> 00:24:22,433
<i>You just stop feeling anything.</i>

316
00:24:23,309 --> 00:24:29,107
<i>Your heart stops, your brain stops,
you rot and return to the earth.</i>

317
00:24:29,732 --> 00:24:32,694
<i>That's what happens
to every living creature.</i>

318
00:24:35,238 --> 00:24:38,449
<i>You're incapable of accepting
such a simple fact.</i>

319
00:24:38,825 --> 00:24:41,452
<i>It must be hard to be so stupid.</i>

320
00:24:42,078 --> 00:24:45,747
<i>I want to bring happiness
to these pitiful people.</i>

321
00:24:45,748 --> 00:24:47,667
<i>I want to save them!</i>

322
00:24:48,293 --> 00:24:50,253
<i>That's why I...</i>

323
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:52,755
<i>was born into this world.</i>

324
00:24:59,262 --> 00:25:00,304
Hmm...

325
00:25:00,305 --> 00:25:01,638
That's the fifth round.

326
00:25:01,639 --> 00:25:03,265
Another dud, huh?

327
00:25:03,266 --> 00:25:04,726
It's not working.

328
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:07,936
It's getting less
and less effective, isn't it?

329
00:25:07,937 --> 00:25:11,524
How many more times
can you mix up that poison?

330
00:25:11,816 --> 00:25:14,110
Oh, are you out of breath now?

331
00:25:14,569 --> 00:25:17,280
Look at all that sweat! Are you all right?

332
00:25:18,072 --> 00:25:19,282
<i>So...</i>

333
00:25:19,657 --> 00:25:21,451
<i>this is the power of an Upper Rank!</i>

334
00:25:21,826 --> 00:25:23,786
<i>The poison's not working on him at all!</i>

335
00:25:24,829 --> 00:25:27,790
<i>The speed at which
he becomes resistant is insane!</i>

336
00:25:30,126 --> 00:25:32,670
Well, the air sacs in your lungs
are going through necrosis.

337
00:25:34,505 --> 00:25:35,798
Painful, isn't it?

338
00:25:36,174 --> 00:25:39,886
You did breathe in
my Blood Demon Art after all.

339
00:25:41,596 --> 00:25:44,431
<i>He turns his frozen blood into mist...</i>

340
00:25:44,432 --> 00:25:46,768
<i>and uses his fans to disperse it.</i>

341
00:25:47,060 --> 00:25:50,563
<i>The very act of breathing itself
becomes dangerous.</i>

342
00:25:58,071 --> 00:25:59,113
<i>I'll use...</i>

343
00:25:59,530 --> 00:26:01,866
<i>consecutive strikes to inject him
with a massive dose of poison!</i>

344
00:26:03,117 --> 00:26:04,493
<i>Insect Breathing...</i>

345
00:26:04,494 --> 00:26:05,995
<i>Dance of the Dragonfly...</i>

346
00:26:12,668 --> 00:26:14,420
<i>Compound Eye Hexagon!</i>

347
00:26:17,382 --> 00:26:18,965
My goodness...

348
00:26:18,966 --> 00:26:20,802
you're incredibly fast!

349
00:26:21,219 --> 00:26:24,931
You might be the fastest Hashira
I've ever met!

350
00:26:28,559 --> 00:26:30,812
<i>I've been... slashed!</i>

351
00:26:33,189 --> 00:26:36,901
If only you could've beheaded me
instead of using poison.

352
00:26:37,026 --> 00:26:39,404
With your speed, you might've beaten me.

353
00:26:41,656 --> 00:26:42,823
Well, maybe not!

354
00:26:42,824 --> 00:26:45,368
Since you're so small!

355
00:26:48,663 --> 00:26:53,000
<i>I wonder why my hands are so small.</i>

356
00:26:53,751 --> 00:26:56,879
<i>Why didn't I ever grow taller?</i>

357
00:26:58,714 --> 00:27:02,135
<i>If I were just a little taller...</i>

358
00:27:02,468 --> 00:27:05,513
<i>could I have beheaded a demon
and defeated it?</i>

359
00:27:06,305 --> 00:27:12,144
<i>Having longer arms and legs means
you have that much more muscle.</i>

360
00:27:12,145 --> 00:27:14,105
<i>That would give me an advantage.</i>

361
00:27:16,524 --> 00:27:18,651
<i>My big sister was petite...</i>

362
00:27:19,318 --> 00:27:21,946
<i>but she was taller than me.</i>

363
00:27:23,322 --> 00:27:26,117
<i>How I envy Mr. Himejima!</i>

364
00:27:26,659 --> 00:27:31,164
<i>Who wouldn't be relieved
to see him come to their rescue?</i>

365
00:27:34,876 --> 00:27:37,753
<i>I know what my sister was trying to say...</i>

366
00:27:38,838 --> 00:27:40,631
<i>that day.</i>

367
00:27:44,093 --> 00:27:47,929
Hey, is this the end?

368
00:27:47,930 --> 00:27:49,557
Too bad, I guess.

369
00:27:53,144 --> 00:27:56,647
<i>"Shinobu, you'll probably lose
to that demon."</i>

370
00:27:57,064 --> 00:28:01,277
<i>That's what you started to say,
but you stopped yourself, right?</i>

371
00:28:01,944 --> 00:28:03,696
<i>Get yourself together.</i>

372
00:28:09,619 --> 00:28:11,954
<i>I won't allow you to shed any tears.</i>

373
00:28:13,039 --> 00:28:14,540
<i>Big Sister...</i>

374
00:28:14,832 --> 00:28:16,000
<i>Stand up.</i>

375
00:28:16,501 --> 00:28:19,252
<i>I can't! I've lost so much blood!</i>

376
00:28:19,253 --> 00:28:23,633
<i>My left lung's punctured,
and I can't even breathe!</i>

377
00:28:23,925 --> 00:28:26,009
<i>I don't want to hear it.</i>

378
00:28:26,010 --> 00:28:27,469
<i>Stand up...</i>

379
00:28:27,470 --> 00:28:29,805
<i>Insect Hashira Shinobu Kocho!</i>

380
00:28:32,225 --> 00:28:34,893
<i>If you've made up your mind
to defeat him, then defeat him!</i>

381
00:28:34,894 --> 00:28:37,480
<i>If you've made up
your mind to win, then win!</i>

382
00:28:38,481 --> 00:28:41,025
<i>Win, whatever it takes.</i>

383
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:45,821
<i>Isn't that what you promised
both me and Kanao?</i>

384
00:28:47,657 --> 00:28:49,242
<i>Kanao...</i>

385
00:28:52,119 --> 00:28:53,620
I'm so sorry...

386
00:28:53,621 --> 00:28:56,165
I didn't finish you off,
so it must really hurt, right?

387
00:29:01,212 --> 00:29:03,588
<i>I know you can do this, Shinobu.</i>

388
00:29:03,589 --> 00:29:05,174
<i>Give it your all.</i>

389
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:15,893
What, you're standing up?
You're really going to stand up? Huh?

390
00:29:16,310 --> 00:29:19,939
Are you... really human?

391
00:29:20,231 --> 00:29:24,402
I slashed your collarbone,
your lung and your ribs.

392
00:29:25,069 --> 00:29:31,993
At your size, the amount of blood
you've lost should've killed you by now.

393
00:29:32,660 --> 00:29:37,081
Oh no, see?
The blood is gurgling in your lungs!

394
00:29:37,415 --> 00:29:40,458
The pain must be unimaginable!

395
00:29:40,459 --> 00:29:44,338
I'll slice off your head right now,
so don't push yourself!

396
00:29:45,381 --> 00:29:47,299
You're past saving now.

397
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:48,967
Go ahead and let go.

398
00:29:48,968 --> 00:29:51,846
<i>I should go for his
Achilles' heel... his neck!</i>

399
00:29:52,138 --> 00:29:55,224
<i>If I slam the poison into his neck,
I'll have a chance!</i>

400
00:29:56,142 --> 00:29:57,892
<i>Insect Breathing...</i>

401
00:29:57,893 --> 00:29:59,645
<i>Dance of the Centipede...</i>

402
00:30:00,313 --> 00:30:01,313
Hmm?

403
00:30:01,314 --> 00:30:03,399
<i>Hundred-legged Zigzag!</i>

404
00:30:26,631 --> 00:30:29,550
<i>She's twisting
and turning in all directions.</i>

405
00:30:29,884 --> 00:30:32,011
<i>The impact of her steps
is enough to destroy the bridge.</i>

406
00:30:35,097 --> 00:30:37,767
<i>So fast! I can't predict her attack!</i>

407
00:30:43,814 --> 00:30:44,815
<i>So low!</i>

408
00:30:58,829 --> 00:31:00,790
<i>The road to bliss.</i>

409
00:31:01,916 --> 00:31:04,001
<i>I always believed...</i>

410
00:31:04,460 --> 00:31:06,504
<i>that it continued to stretch on and on...</i>

411
00:31:07,004 --> 00:31:08,714
<i>far into the distance.</i>

412
00:31:12,301 --> 00:31:14,595
<i>Not until it was destroyed...</i>

413
00:31:15,096 --> 00:31:21,143
<i>did I realize that my bliss
sat on top of a sliver of glass.</i>

414
00:31:23,771 --> 00:31:25,022
<i>And...</i>

415
00:31:25,773 --> 00:31:28,150
<i>just as we'd been rescued...</i>

416
00:31:29,151 --> 00:31:31,362
<i>I wanted to become stronger...</i>

417
00:31:31,696 --> 00:31:33,989
<i>and protect...</i>

418
00:31:34,490 --> 00:31:38,577
<i>someone else's unscathed happiness.</i>

419
00:31:39,995 --> 00:31:41,247
<i>That's what we'd...</i>

420
00:31:42,498 --> 00:31:44,750
<i>promised each other.</i>

421
00:31:46,293 --> 00:31:48,003
<i>"Let's defeat the demons."</i>

422
00:31:48,713 --> 00:31:50,714
<i>"As many as we can."</i>

423
00:31:50,715 --> 00:31:52,341
<i>"Together."</i>

424
00:31:54,927 --> 00:31:57,638
<i>So that others wouldn't have to...</i>

425
00:31:58,305 --> 00:32:01,058
<i>go through what we did!</i>

426
00:32:09,024 --> 00:32:10,735
<i>Even if I'm weak.</i>

427
00:32:14,655 --> 00:32:17,158
<i>Even if I was incapable
of beheading a demon!</i>

428
00:32:17,908 --> 00:32:19,909
<i>By defeating a single demon...</i>

429
00:32:19,910 --> 00:32:21,579
<i>I could save dozens!</i>

430
00:32:21,912 --> 00:32:24,165
<i>And if the demon I brought down
was an Upper Rank...</i>

431
00:32:24,665 --> 00:32:27,752
<i>I could save hundreds of people!</i>

432
00:32:28,836 --> 00:32:30,963
<i>It's not a matter of whether
I can do it or not.</i>

433
00:32:32,590 --> 00:32:35,176
<i>It's something that I have to do.</i>

434
00:32:40,306 --> 00:32:42,308
<i>Are you angry?</i>

435
00:32:43,809 --> 00:32:49,023
<i>Yes, I am angry, Tanjiro.</i>

436
00:32:49,482 --> 00:32:50,983
<i>I'm always...</i>

437
00:32:51,567 --> 00:32:53,860
<i>constantly...</i>

438
00:32:53,861 --> 00:32:55,780
<i>angry.</i>

439
00:32:58,199 --> 00:33:00,451
<i>My parents were killed.</i>

440
00:33:01,577 --> 00:33:03,829
<i>My big sister was killed.</i>

441
00:33:04,914 --> 00:33:08,334
<i>My Tsuguko
other than Kanao were all killed.</i>

442
00:33:09,418 --> 00:33:11,170
<i>Not to mention those girls.</i>

443
00:33:11,962 --> 00:33:14,130
<i>If their loved ones...</i>

444
00:33:14,131 --> 00:33:17,343
<i>hadn't been murdered by demons...</i>

445
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:20,679
<i>they'd still be living happily
with their families!</i>

446
00:33:23,390 --> 00:33:26,393
<i>You make me so livid!</i>

447
00:33:26,727 --> 00:33:28,938
<i>Don't you mess with me, idiot!</i>

448
00:33:30,314 --> 00:33:33,442
<i>Why isn't the poison
working on you, dammit?</i>

449
00:33:34,360 --> 00:33:35,694
<i>You bastard!</i>

450
00:33:47,289 --> 00:33:48,498
So commendable!

451
00:33:48,499 --> 00:33:49,959
You did your best!

452
00:33:50,543 --> 00:33:52,585
My heart is moved!

453
00:33:52,586 --> 00:33:55,756
To see such a weak girl
getting this far...

454
00:33:56,674 --> 00:33:58,633
How did you last this long
as a Demon Slayer...

455
00:33:58,634 --> 00:34:01,720
with less talent than your big sister?

456
00:34:02,179 --> 00:34:05,099
It's a miracle
that you survived until now!

457
00:34:07,351 --> 00:34:09,435
So foolish, you'll try
to see things through

458
00:34:09,436 --> 00:34:11,688
to the end despite the futility!

459
00:34:11,689 --> 00:34:13,898
That's what makes humans so fragile!

460
00:34:13,899 --> 00:34:16,861
And it's what makes humans so magnificent!

461
00:34:17,278 --> 00:34:20,364
You're worthy of being devoured by me!

462
00:34:21,115 --> 00:34:23,367
Let's share eternity, you and I!

463
00:34:26,871 --> 00:34:29,163
Any last words?

464
00:34:29,164 --> 00:34:31,000
I'll be happy to listen.

465
00:34:35,504 --> 00:34:38,132
Go to hell!

466
00:34:43,345 --> 00:34:44,972
Master!

467
00:35:16,253 --> 00:35:18,672
<i>I bet he's here, too.</i>

468
00:35:19,256 --> 00:35:20,925
<i>Since I'm sure...</i>

469
00:35:21,467 --> 00:35:23,302
<i>he also needs to face me!</i>

470
00:35:30,559 --> 00:35:34,228
<i>The people you love and hold dear...</i>

471
00:35:34,229 --> 00:35:35,897
<i>We just thoughtlessly assume</i>

472
00:35:35,898 --> 00:35:38,817
<i>that they'll still be alive tomorrow
and the day after.</i>

473
00:35:39,318 --> 00:35:40,569
<i>But...</i>

474
00:35:41,153 --> 00:35:42,988
<i>that's nothing but a desire.</i>

475
00:35:43,447 --> 00:35:44,949
<i>Flower Breathing...</i>

476
00:35:45,741 --> 00:35:47,033
<i>And even though...</i>

477
00:35:47,034 --> 00:35:49,243
<i>it's not an ironclad promise...</i>

478
00:35:49,244 --> 00:35:50,537
<i>Fourth Form...</i>

479
00:35:52,289 --> 00:35:53,999
<i>Crimson Hanagoromo!</i>

480
00:36:00,589 --> 00:36:03,342
Whoa, that was close!

481
00:36:07,137 --> 00:36:09,556
<i>...they'll always be alive and close by.</i>

482
00:36:11,016 --> 00:36:12,393
<i>For some reason...</i>

483
00:36:12,851 --> 00:36:16,563
<i>people can't help believing that.</i>

484
00:36:19,316 --> 00:36:24,738
Would you mind not attacking me
while I'm absorbing her?

485
00:36:33,539 --> 00:36:34,832
What's this?

486
00:36:35,374 --> 00:36:38,085
You're not taking the bait?

487
00:36:38,752 --> 00:36:43,007
Is it because of what she motioned earlier
with her fingers?

488
00:36:43,382 --> 00:36:46,634
Did she tell you what my powers are?

489
00:36:46,635 --> 00:36:49,805
In just a split second? Amazing!

490
00:36:50,389 --> 00:36:52,057
Even though it's futile.

491
00:36:52,474 --> 00:36:54,685
She's such a hard worker!

492
00:36:57,229 --> 00:36:59,857
But really, I have to say...

493
00:37:00,649 --> 00:37:04,069
what a wonderful night this is.

494
00:37:05,446 --> 00:37:07,363
The feasts just keep coming...

495
00:37:07,364 --> 00:37:10,576
one after another.

496
00:37:11,452 --> 00:37:14,288
Yes, truly...

497
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:17,541
what a wonderful night.

498
00:37:31,180 --> 00:37:32,805
You're here, aren't you?

499
00:37:32,806 --> 00:37:34,141
Show yourself.

500
00:37:35,017 --> 00:37:37,144
I know you're there.

501
00:37:40,314 --> 00:37:43,066
That's no way to talk, you know.

502
00:37:43,067 --> 00:37:45,152
Not to your senior.

503
00:37:46,111 --> 00:37:49,198
You look a little better than before...

504
00:37:49,823 --> 00:37:54,244
but you're still the same
scrawny guy as ever.

505
00:37:57,456 --> 00:37:58,956
{\an8}UPPER SIX

506
00:37:58,957 --> 00:38:01,250
Long time no see...

507
00:38:01,251 --> 00:38:03,212
Zenitsu.

508
00:38:05,881 --> 00:38:07,548
Kaigaku...

509
00:38:07,549 --> 00:38:09,593
Now that you're a demon...

510
00:38:10,260 --> 00:38:13,764
I no longer consider you my senior!

511
00:38:27,236 --> 00:38:28,362
<i>Water Breathing...</i>

512
00:38:28,654 --> 00:38:29,947
<i>Ninth Form...</i>

513
00:38:31,532 --> 00:38:33,534
<i>Splashing Water Flow, Turbulent!</i>

514
00:38:35,994 --> 00:38:37,203
Stay focused!

515
00:38:37,204 --> 00:38:38,497
Right!

516
00:38:39,790 --> 00:38:41,625
<i>This place is crazy!</i>

517
00:38:42,084 --> 00:38:44,418
<i>The buildings themselves are throbbing
like they're pulsing!</i>

518
00:38:44,419 --> 00:38:46,088
<i>It's like it's alive!</i>

519
00:38:46,547 --> 00:38:49,550
<i>It's trying to tear Mr. Giyu and me apart!</i>

520
00:38:50,259 --> 00:38:53,052
<i>We have to reconvene with as many
other Corps members as we can...</i>

521
00:38:53,053 --> 00:38:55,889
<i>and head to where Muzan is!</i>

522
00:39:03,522 --> 00:39:04,939
Deceased!

523
00:39:04,940 --> 00:39:07,025
Shinobu Kocho has died!

524
00:39:07,776 --> 00:39:10,195
After battling Upper Two...

525
00:39:10,571 --> 00:39:12,156
she's now deceased!

526
00:39:53,238 --> 00:39:54,448
<i>That crow...</i>

527
00:39:54,823 --> 00:39:57,159
<i>What's that piece of paper on its neck?</i>

528
00:39:57,534 --> 00:39:59,661
<i>The communications are up so quickly.</i>

529
00:40:03,999 --> 00:40:05,667
Shinobu is dead.

530
00:40:06,168 --> 00:40:08,127
You mustn't look downward.

531
00:40:08,128 --> 00:40:11,172
Just think about
what you're going to do next.

532
00:40:11,173 --> 00:40:12,299
- Right!
- Right!

533
00:40:14,635 --> 00:40:18,388
What's the status of the other Hashira
and Corps members?

534
00:40:20,015 --> 00:40:23,852
At the center of the 40th vertical
and 12th horizontal levels...

535
00:40:25,646 --> 00:40:27,939
the Corps members are fighting demons.

536
00:40:27,940 --> 00:40:30,192
Numbering at least ten.

537
00:40:37,115 --> 00:40:41,453
And beyond that wall,
more than 30 demons are now approaching.

538
00:40:47,918 --> 00:40:52,089
<i>Mr. Yushiro's eyes
can see Blood Demon Arts.</i>

539
00:40:52,464 --> 00:40:56,051
<i>The art itself that is not visible
to human eyes.</i>

540
00:40:56,802 --> 00:40:59,929
<i>These lights of different sizes
must be the potency</i>

541
00:40:59,930 --> 00:41:02,307
<i>of each demon's Blood Demon Art.</i>

542
00:41:03,225 --> 00:41:07,728
<i>And these pulsating buildings
in constant motion...</i>

543
00:41:07,729 --> 00:41:09,606
<i>are also a Blood Demon Art.</i>

544
00:41:09,982 --> 00:41:12,609
<i>And there seems to be no end to it.</i>

545
00:41:15,362 --> 00:41:17,239
<i>Such incredible power.</i>

546
00:41:18,532 --> 00:41:19,824
<i>This is...</i>

547
00:41:19,825 --> 00:41:22,619
<i>a demon castle, spreading out infinitely!</i>

548
00:41:26,248 --> 00:41:30,460
<i>And we have been lured
inside this infinite demon castle.</i>

549
00:41:34,548 --> 00:41:35,756
<i>But...</i>

550
00:41:35,757 --> 00:41:38,218
<i>it's not as if we were just drawn in.</i>

551
00:41:38,635 --> 00:41:40,679
<i>My father prepared
for this day meticulously...</i>

552
00:41:41,054 --> 00:41:42,514
<i>and here we are now.</i>

553
00:41:43,557 --> 00:41:45,349
<i>Using Gyomei as the linchpin...</i>

554
00:41:45,350 --> 00:41:49,104
<i>he had the Hashira positioned
to arrive on the scene at any time...</i>

555
00:41:49,438 --> 00:41:52,356
<i>and in order to align
all of the individual Corps members...</i>

556
00:41:52,357 --> 00:41:56,236
<i>he gave the Kasugai Crows
their missions and waited.</i>

557
00:41:57,154 --> 00:42:00,573
<i>Enlisting the aid
of both Ms. Tamayo and Mr. Yushiro...</i>

558
00:42:00,574 --> 00:42:01,742
<i>and finally...</i>

559
00:42:02,284 --> 00:42:04,911
<i>to ensure that this plan
would be perfect...</i>

560
00:42:05,329 --> 00:42:07,331
<i>my sisters also sacrificed their lives...</i>

561
00:42:08,206 --> 00:42:10,709
<i>along with those of our parents.</i>

562
00:42:13,920 --> 00:42:15,339
We will not...

563
00:42:15,964 --> 00:42:17,341
lose this battle!

564
00:42:23,764 --> 00:42:28,976
<i>Five massive powers are being emitted
throughout this great space...</i>

565
00:42:28,977 --> 00:42:31,313
<i>as if flaunting their own strength.</i>

566
00:42:31,688 --> 00:42:33,774
<i>These must be the Upper Ranks.</i>

567
00:42:34,733 --> 00:42:38,903
<i>One of them is at the same spot
where Shinobu was located.</i>

568
00:42:38,904 --> 00:42:40,279
Upper Rank sighting!

569
00:42:40,280 --> 00:42:43,449
Upper Six and Agatsuma
have encountered each other!

570
00:42:43,450 --> 00:42:46,369
An Upper Rank! Are there
any other Corps members with him?

571
00:42:46,370 --> 00:42:48,997
None! Agatsuma is alone!

572
00:42:49,289 --> 00:42:51,874
The odds aren't good for a lone Hinoe!

573
00:42:51,875 --> 00:42:53,418
Send him backup right away!

574
00:43:00,008 --> 00:43:02,134
You haven't changed, have you?

575
00:43:02,135 --> 00:43:04,303
You're still a runt and shabby-looking...

576
00:43:04,304 --> 00:43:06,890
and weak as ever.

577
00:43:07,557 --> 00:43:09,810
Were you able to become a Hashira?

578
00:43:10,310 --> 00:43:13,438
Hey, Zenitsu!

579
00:43:13,814 --> 00:43:17,984
Did you ever learn to use
anything besides the First Form?

580
00:43:18,735 --> 00:43:20,861
Someone seems thrilled to have made it

581
00:43:20,862 --> 00:43:25,075
as an Upper Rank
bottom-feeder as a stopgap.

582
00:43:25,909 --> 00:43:27,494
Hah!

583
00:43:28,537 --> 00:43:31,623
You sure learned to mouth off.

584
00:43:32,374 --> 00:43:34,918
Why did you become a demon of all things?

585
00:43:36,044 --> 00:43:37,086
You would never--

586
00:43:37,087 --> 00:43:41,091
Why would the prospective heir
of Thunder Breathing become a demon?

587
00:43:42,592 --> 00:43:43,717
Huh?

588
00:43:43,718 --> 00:43:45,970
Because you turned into a demon...

589
00:43:45,971 --> 00:43:47,931
Gramps...

590
00:43:49,224 --> 00:43:51,226
committed seppuku and died!

591
00:43:52,394 --> 00:43:53,812
Gramps...

592
00:43:54,271 --> 00:43:56,314
committed seppuku alone!

593
00:43:57,607 --> 00:43:59,985
Without any assistance!

594
00:44:00,569 --> 00:44:02,153
If you don't have
someone cut off your head

595
00:44:02,154 --> 00:44:04,530
after you've stabbed
yourself in the belly...

596
00:44:04,531 --> 00:44:07,491
you die a drawn-out death in agony!

597
00:44:07,492 --> 00:44:08,951
Gramps...

598
00:44:08,952 --> 00:44:12,455
died without even stabbing
his own throat or heart!

599
00:44:12,456 --> 00:44:16,084
All because a demon was produced
from a Thunder Breathing user!

600
00:44:17,419 --> 00:44:19,546
What do I care?

601
00:44:19,963 --> 00:44:22,465
So? What is it?

602
00:44:22,466 --> 00:44:24,049
You want me to grieve?

603
00:44:24,050 --> 00:44:26,302
To repent and atone for my ways?

604
00:44:26,303 --> 00:44:31,308
I have no use for anyone
who doesn't value me.

605
00:44:31,808 --> 00:44:33,143
I always...

606
00:44:33,643 --> 00:44:35,227
no matter what...

607
00:44:35,228 --> 00:44:38,523
take the side of whoever knows my worth.

608
00:44:40,275 --> 00:44:44,528
If the old geezer died in agony, I'm glad.

609
00:44:44,529 --> 00:44:47,491
After all that I did for him...

610
00:44:47,908 --> 00:44:49,909
instead of making me his successor...

611
00:44:49,910 --> 00:44:55,290
he had the gall to make trash like you
my co-successor, that bastard!

612
00:44:56,124 --> 00:44:58,001
Former Hashira or not...

613
00:44:58,293 --> 00:45:01,880
I have no use for a senile geezer!

614
00:45:06,760 --> 00:45:09,554
Gramps wasn't senile by a long shot.

615
00:45:09,930 --> 00:45:12,933
If I'm trash, then you're scum!

616
00:45:13,308 --> 00:45:15,434
Between me, who could
only use the First Form,

617
00:45:15,435 --> 00:45:18,313
and you, who could
never use the First Form...

618
00:45:19,022 --> 00:45:23,317
I feel sorry for Gramps to have
such a sorry pair of successors!

619
00:45:23,318 --> 00:45:25,319
Don't lump me together...

620
00:45:25,320 --> 00:45:27,280
with the likes of you!

621
00:45:27,864 --> 00:45:29,198
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

622
00:45:29,199 --> 00:45:30,533
<i>Fourth Form...</i>

623
00:45:30,534 --> 00:45:31,785
<i>Distant Thunder!</i>

624
00:45:40,126 --> 00:45:42,254
You're too slow, scum.

625
00:45:47,801 --> 00:45:49,426
<i>He slashed me!</i>

626
00:45:49,427 --> 00:45:50,636
<i>So fast!</i>

627
00:45:50,637 --> 00:45:52,180
<i>He's...</i>

628
00:45:52,514 --> 00:45:56,434
<i>moving like a totally different person!</i>

629
00:45:58,103 --> 00:46:00,480
<i>I'm not wrong!</i>

630
00:46:10,824 --> 00:46:15,078
<i>There's no shame in kneeling down
before the overwhelmingly powerful.</i>

631
00:46:16,079 --> 00:46:19,541
<i>As long as you're alive,
you'll find a way.</i>

632
00:46:21,501 --> 00:46:24,879
<i>You haven't lost until the moment you die.</i>

633
00:46:25,171 --> 00:46:28,133
<i>Whether you grovel on the ground...</i>

634
00:46:28,466 --> 00:46:30,301
<i>whether you have no home...</i>

635
00:46:30,302 --> 00:46:32,512
<i>and have to drink from a puddle...</i>

636
00:46:32,887 --> 00:46:36,391
<i>whether they condemn you
for stealing money...</i>

637
00:46:36,933 --> 00:46:40,352
<i>as long as you're alive,
you can win some day.</i>

638
00:46:40,353 --> 00:46:41,937
<i>I'll win and prove it.</i>

639
00:46:41,938 --> 00:46:44,774
<i>Believing that has kept me going in life.</i>

640
00:46:46,776 --> 00:46:48,737
<i>Do you wish to gain even more power...</i>

641
00:46:49,696 --> 00:46:52,574
<i>by becoming a demon?</i>

642
00:46:53,283 --> 00:46:56,577
<i>Should that man acknowledge you...</i>

643
00:46:56,578 --> 00:46:59,873
<i>then you, too, will become one of us.</i>

644
00:47:03,668 --> 00:47:05,670
<i>The stronger the swordsman...</i>

645
00:47:06,254 --> 00:47:09,466
<i>the longer it takes for him
to become a demon.</i>

646
00:47:09,924 --> 00:47:13,386
<i>It took me three full days.</i>

647
00:47:13,928 --> 00:47:17,557
<i>Turning a wielder
of a Breathing Technique into a demon...</i>

648
00:47:17,974 --> 00:47:23,438
<i>will require a massive amount
of that man's blood.</i>

649
00:47:24,022 --> 00:47:25,982
<i>And though rare...</i>

650
00:47:26,274 --> 00:47:31,404
<i>some are physically
incapable of becoming demons...</i>

651
00:47:31,905 --> 00:47:34,658
<i>I wonder how you will fare.</i>

652
00:47:38,703 --> 00:47:41,164
<i>You must appreciate this blood.</i>

653
00:47:41,581 --> 00:47:45,585
<i>Do not even think
of spilling a single drop.</i>

654
00:47:46,419 --> 00:47:48,672
<i>Should you let any fall...</i>

655
00:47:49,089 --> 00:47:51,882
<i>your head and torso...</i>

656
00:47:51,883 --> 00:47:53,927
<i>will be severed.</i>

657
00:47:59,349 --> 00:48:02,560
<i>That terror that felt
like every cell in my body...</i>

658
00:48:02,894 --> 00:48:06,022
<i>was screaming and sobbing...</i>

659
00:48:10,485 --> 00:48:12,404
<i>Compared to that...</i>

660
00:48:12,696 --> 00:48:15,990
<i>this little punk is nothing!</i>

661
00:48:16,491 --> 00:48:20,078
<i>Just 'cause he's stronger doesn't mean
he's on par with an Upper Rank!</i>

662
00:48:20,995 --> 00:48:24,540
<i>Zenitsu Agatsuma... This guy is trash!</i>

663
00:48:24,541 --> 00:48:27,000
<i>He was always sniveling like a baby!</i>

664
00:48:27,001 --> 00:48:29,713
<i>Not a shred of dignity or grit!</i>

665
00:48:30,088 --> 00:48:31,797
<i>Help me!</i>

666
00:48:31,798 --> 00:48:33,841
<i>There's a pitfall!</i>

667
00:48:33,842 --> 00:48:36,553
<i>I twisted my ankle!</i>

668
00:48:37,011 --> 00:48:42,517
<i>Me, co-successor with this trash?
That damn geezer was full of it!</i>

669
00:48:43,059 --> 00:48:45,019
<i>Here you go, Kaigaku.</i>

670
00:48:45,812 --> 00:48:48,106
<i>Gramps!</i>

671
00:48:48,690 --> 00:48:51,443
<i>It's a little too big, see?</i>

672
00:48:51,735 --> 00:48:55,321
- <i>Come on, Gramps!
- You and me, equals?</i>

673
00:48:57,490 --> 00:48:59,951
There's just no way in hell!

674
00:49:01,453 --> 00:49:04,413
He deserved to die!

675
00:49:04,414 --> 00:49:06,498
That goes for both you
and that old geezer!

676
00:49:06,499 --> 00:49:09,461
You both deserve to die!

677
00:49:10,295 --> 00:49:13,339
<i>I could only learn the First Form...</i>

678
00:49:13,965 --> 00:49:17,677
<i>and you were able to learn
everything but the First Form.</i>

679
00:49:19,679 --> 00:49:21,306
<i>That's why Gramps...</i>

680
00:49:21,723 --> 00:49:27,103
<i>wanted us both to be
his Thunder Breathing successors.</i>

681
00:49:28,938 --> 00:49:31,399
<i>But you wanted so badly
to deny him that...</i>

682
00:49:31,900 --> 00:49:35,612
<i>you became a demon, didn't you?</i>

683
00:49:37,864 --> 00:49:38,864
<i>Here it comes!</i>

684
00:49:38,865 --> 00:49:40,324
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

685
00:49:40,325 --> 00:49:41,493
<i>Second Form...</i>

686
00:49:42,619 --> 00:49:43,828
<i>Rice Spirit!</i>

687
00:49:46,080 --> 00:49:49,334
<i>With one breath, five flashes
in the blink of an eye!</i>

688
00:49:51,795 --> 00:49:53,630
You must've devoured tons of people!

689
00:49:53,922 --> 00:49:56,841
You can't even tell right from wrong
any more, can you?

690
00:49:57,133 --> 00:49:59,385
Oh, I know the difference
between right and wrong!

691
00:50:01,137 --> 00:50:02,263
What's the matter?

692
00:50:02,680 --> 00:50:05,600
Aren't you the old geezer's favorite?

693
00:50:06,643 --> 00:50:09,479
So, why don't you show me...

694
00:50:09,771 --> 00:50:12,357
what he graciously passed down to you?

695
00:50:15,985 --> 00:50:17,486
What's wrong?

696
00:50:17,487 --> 00:50:19,322
Don't hold back!

697
00:50:19,614 --> 00:50:21,825
Just hit me with it already!

698
00:50:28,206 --> 00:50:29,666
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

699
00:50:32,210 --> 00:50:33,461
<i>First Form...</i>

700
00:50:35,630 --> 00:50:37,340
<i>Thunderclap and Flash!</i>

701
00:50:43,680 --> 00:50:46,932
Such a basic move where all you do
is charge at me head-on...

702
00:50:46,933 --> 00:50:48,642
so brainlessly...

703
00:50:48,643 --> 00:50:50,228
could never hit me!

704
00:50:52,063 --> 00:50:53,481
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

705
00:50:53,815 --> 00:50:55,190
<i>Third Form...</i>

706
00:50:55,191 --> 00:50:56,734
<i>Thunder Swarm!</i>

707
00:51:02,782 --> 00:51:04,951
<i>He's attacking me in waves while spinning!</i>

708
00:51:05,243 --> 00:51:06,702
What's wrong?

709
00:51:06,703 --> 00:51:08,454
Are you done already?

710
00:51:10,039 --> 00:51:11,039
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

711
00:51:11,040 --> 00:51:12,291
<i>First Form...</i>

712
00:51:12,292 --> 00:51:13,835
<i>Thunderclap and Flash! Eightfold!</i>

713
00:51:19,090 --> 00:51:21,217
It's not working!

714
00:51:21,968 --> 00:51:23,177
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

715
00:51:23,928 --> 00:51:25,054
<i>Fifth Form...</i>

716
00:51:27,557 --> 00:51:28,933
<i>Heat Lightning!</i>

717
00:51:30,810 --> 00:51:31,978
How does it feel?

718
00:51:32,812 --> 00:51:36,232
The bite of my
Blood Demon Art-enhanced sword?

719
00:51:36,774 --> 00:51:39,068
A deadly strike that cracks...

720
00:51:39,360 --> 00:51:41,571
and burns your skin and flesh!

721
00:51:42,614 --> 00:51:45,950
Those who correctly evaluate
and recognize my value are good!

722
00:51:46,701 --> 00:51:49,704
Those who write me off
and fail to acknowledge me are evil!

723
00:51:50,580 --> 00:51:51,830
Do you get it now?

724
00:51:51,831 --> 00:51:54,292
This is my power now!

725
00:51:54,709 --> 00:51:56,628
The power I gained
by becoming a demon, that is!

726
00:51:57,211 --> 00:51:59,212
Single thunderclap or eightfold or what...

727
00:51:59,213 --> 00:52:02,216
making you his successor
when that's all you can do...

728
00:52:02,508 --> 00:52:04,135
was a total misjudgment!

729
00:52:11,559 --> 00:52:15,521
So, that's the answer
you've come up with, huh?

730
00:52:17,273 --> 00:52:19,274
I knew it.

731
00:52:19,275 --> 00:52:21,152
I always knew it, but still...

732
00:52:26,157 --> 00:52:27,574
Zenitsu!

733
00:52:27,575 --> 00:52:28,825
This...

734
00:52:28,826 --> 00:52:30,119
is the end!

735
00:52:30,578 --> 00:52:32,121
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

736
00:52:33,498 --> 00:52:35,124
<i>Sixth Form...</i>

737
00:52:43,758 --> 00:52:46,052
<i>Rumble and Flash!</i>

738
00:52:46,511 --> 00:52:50,014
That strike will keep cracking
throughout your body!

739
00:52:50,306 --> 00:52:52,349
Burn it into your mind and body!

740
00:52:52,350 --> 00:52:54,018
My power!

741
00:52:54,310 --> 00:52:57,522
Now that I'm a demon,
I've surpassed Thunder Breathing!

742
00:53:02,068 --> 00:53:03,610
I'm special!

743
00:53:03,611 --> 00:53:05,196
I'm not like you!

744
00:53:05,571 --> 00:53:07,949
I'm not like any of you!

745
00:53:08,491 --> 00:53:11,953
It looks like the old geezer
struck out with you after all!

746
00:53:16,541 --> 00:53:19,376
<i>Be more like Kaigaku!</i>

747
00:53:19,377 --> 00:53:23,089
<i>Try to be like your senior!</i>

748
00:53:23,548 --> 00:53:28,010
<i>Isn't the First Form the entire basis
of Thunder Breathing?</i>

749
00:53:28,011 --> 00:53:32,806
<i>If the First Form's the only one
he can't use, doesn't that mean... Y'know?</i>

750
00:53:32,807 --> 00:53:36,810
<i>He may have mastered other forms,
but he's no big deal.</i>

751
00:53:36,811 --> 00:53:40,940
<i>But even still,
that Kaigaku guy's so arrogant.</i>

752
00:53:41,315 --> 00:53:43,567
<i>No way can he become a Hashira.</i>

753
00:53:43,568 --> 00:53:46,154
<i>He'll probably croak right away anyway.</i>

754
00:53:46,654 --> 00:53:49,449
<i>Wh-What do you think you're doing?</i>

755
00:53:50,450 --> 00:53:53,202
<i>I hear you punched
a higher-ranking Corps member.</i>

756
00:53:53,703 --> 00:53:55,955
<i>Don't go around making trouble, you trash!</i>

757
00:53:56,748 --> 00:54:00,835
<i>How shameful that someone like you exists!</i>

758
00:54:02,837 --> 00:54:07,258
<i>I was fully aware that Kaigaku hated me...</i>

759
00:54:07,633 --> 00:54:10,344
<i>and I hated him right back.</i>

760
00:54:11,054 --> 00:54:13,597
<i>But I respected you.</i>

761
00:54:13,598 --> 00:54:15,141
<i>I truly did.</i>

762
00:54:15,600 --> 00:54:19,395
<i>You were such a hard worker,
and you kept grinding away.</i>

763
00:54:19,896 --> 00:54:23,775
<i>I always looked up to you as an example.</i>

764
00:54:24,442 --> 00:54:27,236
<i>You were special, you know.</i>

765
00:54:28,488 --> 00:54:33,117
<i>For both Gramps and me,
you were special and important!</i>

766
00:54:33,743 --> 00:54:34,868
<i>But...</i>

767
00:54:34,869 --> 00:54:37,121
<i>I guess that wasn't enough for you.</i>

768
00:54:37,955 --> 00:54:39,624
<i>No matter what...</i>

769
00:54:40,249 --> 00:54:42,960
<i>I always heard a sound
of discontent from you.</i>

770
00:54:45,004 --> 00:54:50,051
<i>There's a hole in the box
where you store the joy in your heart.</i>

771
00:54:51,094 --> 00:54:53,679
<i>And the joy just keeps leaking out.</i>

772
00:54:55,056 --> 00:54:57,974
<i>You have to spot the hole
and close it up...</i>

773
00:54:57,975 --> 00:55:00,019
<i>or the box will never be filled.</i>

774
00:55:02,647 --> 00:55:03,981
<i>Gramps...</i>

775
00:55:04,565 --> 00:55:05,775
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

776
00:55:06,734 --> 00:55:08,653
<i>We ended up...</i>

777
00:55:09,862 --> 00:55:11,447
<i>taking different paths!</i>

778
00:55:22,792 --> 00:55:24,418
<i>He still has some strength left?</i>

779
00:55:34,011 --> 00:55:35,930
<i>Wh-What the hell?</i>

780
00:55:43,813 --> 00:55:44,981
<i>Sorry...</i>

781
00:55:45,982 --> 00:55:47,024
<i>Big Brother.</i>

782
00:56:07,086 --> 00:56:08,462
<i>Thunder Breathing...</i>

783
00:56:08,921 --> 00:56:10,548
<i>Seventh Form...</i>

784
00:56:13,676 --> 00:56:15,553
<i>God of Fire Thunder!</i>

785
00:56:23,060 --> 00:56:24,228
<i>I...</i>

786
00:56:25,062 --> 00:56:26,564
<i>I couldn't see that coming!</i>

787
00:56:26,898 --> 00:56:29,192
<i>What the hell is that move?</i>

788
00:56:29,859 --> 00:56:31,235
<i>It's too fast!</i>

789
00:56:31,569 --> 00:56:34,906
<i>I've never seen that technique!
What the hell did you just use?</i>

790
00:56:35,281 --> 00:56:37,908
<i>Dammit! Dammit!</i>

791
00:56:37,909 --> 00:56:40,952
I knew that old fart always favored you!

792
00:56:40,953 --> 00:56:44,247
He only taught you that technique
and never showed me!

793
00:56:44,248 --> 00:56:45,875
You're wrong!

794
00:56:48,127 --> 00:56:51,047
Gramps wasn't that kind of man!

795
00:56:51,672 --> 00:56:54,425
It's my own technique.

796
00:56:54,967 --> 00:56:58,346
My own exclusive technique
that I came up with myself.

797
00:56:58,930 --> 00:57:00,056
I was hoping to one day...

798
00:57:01,307 --> 00:57:03,225
use this technique...

799
00:57:03,226 --> 00:57:06,520
to battle by your side.

800
00:57:10,024 --> 00:57:12,318
<i>A seventh technique?</i>

801
00:57:12,902 --> 00:57:18,574
<i>Thunder Breathing only has six techniques,
and he created a seventh?</i>

802
00:57:19,408 --> 00:57:20,992
<i>Him?</i>

803
00:57:20,993 --> 00:57:23,788
<i>A guy who can only use the First Form?</i>

804
00:57:24,538 --> 00:57:27,291
<i>That trash who's inferior to me?</i>

805
00:57:29,126 --> 00:57:31,753
<i>I can't take it! I just can't take it!</i>

806
00:57:31,754 --> 00:57:34,465
<i>No way can I accept that as a fact!</i>

807
00:57:34,966 --> 00:57:38,302
<i>A guy like that... Me, lose to him?</i>

808
00:57:39,553 --> 00:57:42,223
<i>I think I'm losing my mind!</i>

809
00:57:43,641 --> 00:57:44,642
<i>No...</i>

810
00:57:45,685 --> 00:57:47,727
<i>Wait, it's not a loss!</i>

811
00:57:47,728 --> 00:57:50,146
<i>That trash is going to fall
with me and die, too!</i>

812
00:57:50,147 --> 00:57:52,817
<i>His strength's depleted by now for sure!</i>

813
00:57:53,734 --> 00:57:56,237
<i>He's going to die along with me!</i>

814
00:57:57,780 --> 00:58:02,285
Those who don't give to others
end up never receiving from others.

815
00:58:03,828 --> 00:58:08,082
Guys who do nothing but want
are the same as those who possess nothing.

816
00:58:08,833 --> 00:58:11,919
Because they can't
produce anything themselves.

817
00:58:13,212 --> 00:58:16,340
Dying alone is pathetic, huh?

818
00:58:38,321 --> 00:58:39,697
<i>Where am I?</i>

819
00:58:48,247 --> 00:58:49,874
<i>Gramps!</i>

820
00:58:52,335 --> 00:58:55,921
<i>Sorry! I couldn't get along with Kaigaku!</i>

821
00:58:56,255 --> 00:58:58,089
<i>I did write him letters and stuff!</i>

822
00:58:58,090 --> 00:59:00,926
<i>But he never replied!</i>

823
00:59:01,594 --> 00:59:05,681
<i>If it weren't for me,
Kaigaku might not have ended up like that!</i>

824
00:59:06,015 --> 00:59:08,392
<i>I'm really sorry! Forgive me!</i>

825
00:59:09,143 --> 00:59:11,936
<i>Sorry that I couldn't pay you back
for all that you did for me!</i>

826
00:59:11,937 --> 00:59:16,150
<i>I wanted to become a Hashira
while you were alive, but...</i>

827
00:59:16,734 --> 00:59:17,817
<i>Sorry!</i>

828
00:59:17,818 --> 00:59:20,112
<i>Sorry, Gramps!</i>

829
00:59:23,699 --> 00:59:25,618
<i>Do you hate me now?</i>

830
00:59:26,410 --> 00:59:29,121
<i>Please! Say something, Gramps!</i>

831
00:59:30,623 --> 00:59:31,706
<i>Dammit!</i>

832
00:59:31,707 --> 00:59:33,959
<i>What's this grabbing onto my legs?</i>

833
00:59:35,544 --> 00:59:38,714
<i>Gramps! I... I...</i>

834
00:59:40,800 --> 00:59:42,343
<i>Dammit!</i>

835
00:59:44,428 --> 00:59:46,180
<i>Zenitsu...</i>

836
00:59:53,729 --> 00:59:57,900
<i>You're my pride and joy.</i>

837
01:00:20,381 --> 01:00:21,382
Well?

838
01:00:21,674 --> 01:00:23,050
Can you save him?

839
01:00:23,342 --> 01:00:26,178
He's my acquaintance!
Find a way to save him!

840
01:00:26,595 --> 01:00:27,930
I'm really counting on you!

841
01:00:28,305 --> 01:00:30,266
Quiet down. Shut up, Murata.

842
01:00:30,641 --> 01:00:32,768
A lowly scrub like you...

843
01:00:33,144 --> 01:00:35,771
Better keep watch
so we don't get attacked.

844
01:00:37,148 --> 01:00:39,274
Hey you! What rank are you?

845
01:00:39,275 --> 01:00:41,861
If you're below me,
there'll be hell to pay!

846
01:00:42,570 --> 01:00:46,449
<i>I'm a demon,
so what do I care about ranks?</i>

847
01:00:46,907 --> 01:00:48,533
I'm using a Blood Demon styptic...

848
01:00:48,534 --> 01:00:51,286
but if these cracks on
his face keep spreading,

849
01:00:51,287 --> 01:00:53,372
it's going to rip all the
way to his eyeballs.

850
01:00:54,373 --> 01:00:55,916
Can you hear me?

851
01:01:00,129 --> 01:01:02,465
Don't say scary things
to someone so vulnerable!

852
01:01:02,923 --> 01:01:06,176
I'm also using a hemostatic,
but the bleeding won't stop.

853
01:01:06,177 --> 01:01:07,427
Stop it!

854
01:01:07,428 --> 01:01:09,512
I swear you'll be fine!
You'll be saved for sure!

855
01:01:09,513 --> 01:01:11,055
You're not gonna die!

856
01:01:11,056 --> 01:01:12,432
You can do it, Agatsuma!

857
01:01:12,433 --> 01:01:13,893
Hang in there! Hang in there!

858
01:01:14,852 --> 01:01:17,061
The Upper Rank that you fought

859
01:01:17,062 --> 01:01:20,566
still hadn't mastered
his techniques and abilities.

860
01:01:20,983 --> 01:01:22,943
That was a lucky break for you.

861
01:01:23,736 --> 01:01:27,239
If you'd fought him a year from now,
you probably would've died instantly.

862
01:01:28,991 --> 01:01:30,700
Stop saying stuff...

863
01:01:30,701 --> 01:01:32,953
that will crush his soul!

864
01:01:39,668 --> 01:01:43,088
I-I didn't say anything wrong!

865
01:01:44,590 --> 01:01:45,966
Wh-What?

866
01:01:46,550 --> 01:01:48,802
You yelled, so now the demons are coming.

867
01:01:50,930 --> 01:01:52,348
You make a good target.

868
01:01:54,141 --> 01:01:57,810
Hey, was your name Yushiro?
I'm leaving Agatsuma in your hands!

869
01:01:57,811 --> 01:01:58,938
Come on!

870
01:02:02,399 --> 01:02:04,734
Please defeat it
as fast as you can, Senpai.

871
01:02:04,735 --> 01:02:07,028
I'm going to give you
such an earful later!

872
01:02:07,029 --> 01:02:08,113
Dammit!

873
01:02:10,199 --> 01:02:12,451
<i>Water Breathing, Second Form...</i>

874
01:02:12,993 --> 01:02:14,036
<i>Water Wheel!</i>

875
01:02:17,248 --> 01:02:20,543
We're going to head them off,
so go from that direction!

876
01:02:37,142 --> 01:02:40,104
<i>Not good! They're going to run into one!</i>

877
01:02:43,482 --> 01:02:45,818
<i>We're not running into any Upper Ranks.</i>

878
01:02:46,193 --> 01:02:48,820
<i>Are we still far off from where Muzan is?</i>

879
01:02:48,821 --> 01:02:51,115
<i>Are the others still alive?</i>

880
01:02:53,826 --> 01:02:55,286
<i>Ms. Shinobu...</i>

881
01:02:56,412 --> 01:02:58,371
<i>We're going to win for sure!</i>

882
01:02:58,372 --> 01:02:59,998
<i>Everyone will!</i>

883
01:02:59,999 --> 01:03:01,625
<i>We all will!</i>

884
01:03:03,919 --> 01:03:05,421
What's this shaking?

885
01:03:05,879 --> 01:03:06,880
M-Mr. Giyu!

886
01:03:07,631 --> 01:03:08,632
Stop!

887
01:03:09,091 --> 01:03:10,259
Calm down.

888
01:03:12,469 --> 01:03:14,388
<i>Is someone else fighting?</i>

889
01:03:14,763 --> 01:03:16,849
<i>Is someone else about to die?</i>

890
01:03:22,938 --> 01:03:24,648
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

891
01:03:24,982 --> 01:03:27,359
<i>Is it coming this way?</i>

892
01:03:29,737 --> 01:03:32,197
<i>Th-This scent...</i>

893
01:03:40,664 --> 01:03:42,416
Above you! Tanjiro, fall back!

894
01:03:47,212 --> 01:03:49,131
Long time no see.

895
01:03:50,841 --> 01:03:53,552
I'm surprised you're still alive.

896
01:03:54,178 --> 01:03:56,471
A weakling like you...

897
01:03:56,472 --> 01:03:57,556
{\an8}UPPER THREE

898
01:03:58,265 --> 01:03:59,433
Tanjiro...

899
01:03:59,767 --> 01:04:01,185
Kamado!

900
01:04:03,437 --> 01:04:06,774
Akaza!

901
01:04:38,972 --> 01:04:40,306
<i>Most likely...</i>

902
01:04:40,307 --> 01:04:44,102
<i>he's decomposing the drug
to turn him back</i>

903
01:04:44,103 --> 01:04:47,981
<i>into a human inside this flesh cocoon.</i>

904
01:04:48,732 --> 01:04:50,442
<i>Muzan Kibutsuji...</i>

905
01:04:50,943 --> 01:04:52,485
<i>No matter what...</i>

906
01:04:52,486 --> 01:04:55,280
<i>you absolutely must be destroyed!</i>

907
01:04:56,407 --> 01:04:58,157
<i>And yet...</i>

908
01:04:58,158 --> 01:04:59,827
<i>no matter what I do...</i>

909
01:05:07,793 --> 01:05:09,127
<i>Eventually...</i>

910
01:05:09,128 --> 01:05:11,380
<i>I'll be absorbed into him, as well!</i>

911
01:05:12,214 --> 01:05:13,589
<i>Please...</i>

912
01:05:13,590 --> 01:05:14,674
<i>somebody...</i>

913
01:05:14,675 --> 01:05:16,260
<i>come soon!</i>

914
01:05:17,469 --> 01:05:18,804
<i>Please!</i>

915
01:05:33,193 --> 01:05:38,657
<i>According to Father, should Muzan die,
the other demons will also die.</i>

916
01:05:40,242 --> 01:05:44,288
<i>In that case,
Muzan Kibutsuji is still alive.</i>

917
01:05:45,581 --> 01:05:49,835
<i>Ms. Tamayo must be suppressing
Muzan's powers.</i>

918
01:05:50,794 --> 01:05:53,004
<i>It's because she's suppressing them</i>

919
01:05:53,005 --> 01:05:55,799
<i>that he hasn't reacted
to Mr. Yushiro's eyes.</i>

920
01:05:56,717 --> 01:05:59,886
<i>Before Muzan's powers are revived...</i>

921
01:05:59,887 --> 01:06:02,598
<i>we must do whatever it takes
to defeat him.</i>

922
01:06:04,349 --> 01:06:05,726
<i>Still...</i>

923
01:06:06,101 --> 01:06:07,227
<i>inside this...</i>

924
01:06:07,561 --> 01:06:09,646
<i>infinite castle...</i>

925
01:06:10,481 --> 01:06:14,610
<i>can we really find Muzan Kibutsuji?</i>

926
01:06:19,782 --> 01:06:21,700
<i>No need to panic.</i>

927
01:06:22,326 --> 01:06:24,703
<i>You're doing a good job.</i>

928
01:06:26,622 --> 01:06:30,000
<i>He will show himself without fail.</i>

929
01:06:30,459 --> 01:06:33,170
<i>Didn't he come to me, as well?</i>

930
01:06:35,339 --> 01:06:37,673
<i>That's the kind of man...</i>

931
01:06:37,674 --> 01:06:40,594
<i>Muzan Kibutsuji is.</i>

932
01:06:45,432 --> 01:06:46,599
<i>Understood...</i>

933
01:06:46,600 --> 01:06:47,851
<i>Father.</i>

934
01:06:48,185 --> 01:06:50,771
<i>I will fulfill my duty, no matter what!</i>

935
01:06:52,439 --> 01:06:55,734
<i>We must find him before the Corps members'
strength is depleted...</i>

936
01:06:56,109 --> 01:06:57,986
<i>and settle this once and for all!</i>

937
01:07:09,164 --> 01:07:10,790
Shield them!

938
01:07:10,791 --> 01:07:15,711
We're going to stand our ground
and minimize the damage to the Hashira!

939
01:07:15,712 --> 01:07:18,215
Ahead! Please go on ahead!

940
01:07:18,882 --> 01:07:20,883
Stone Hashira, please hurry!

941
01:07:20,884 --> 01:07:22,010
You guys...

942
01:07:30,727 --> 01:07:33,145
Whatever you do, please defeat Kibutsuji!

943
01:07:33,146 --> 01:07:34,565
Please!

944
01:07:35,399 --> 01:07:36,691
All right.

945
01:07:36,692 --> 01:07:39,610
I'm counting on you all to deal with this!

946
01:07:39,611 --> 01:07:41,196
Tokito!

947
01:07:42,739 --> 01:07:46,534
Now's the time to prove
what we gained from Hashira Training!

948
01:07:46,535 --> 01:07:47,911
Right!

949
01:07:55,085 --> 01:07:57,379
<i>Thanks, all of you.</i>

950
01:07:58,088 --> 01:08:01,717
<i>Father, everyone's giving it their all.</i>

951
01:08:12,436 --> 01:08:13,770
No crying.

952
01:08:14,563 --> 01:08:16,481
Don't stop what you're doing,
no matter what.

953
01:08:16,940 --> 01:08:19,568
We're not going down in defeat.

954
01:08:21,069 --> 01:08:22,237
Right.

955
01:08:25,449 --> 01:08:28,994
Lord Kiriya is so commendable.

956
01:08:29,912 --> 01:08:33,081
He's still in anguish
over the loss of his father...

957
01:08:33,457 --> 01:08:35,918
yet he's assumed command
of the Demon Slayer Corps...

958
01:08:36,293 --> 01:08:39,588
and is working to fulfill his duty.

959
01:08:41,089 --> 01:08:43,884
Am I right, Mr. Rengoku?

960
01:08:45,052 --> 01:08:46,595
I agree.

961
01:08:48,180 --> 01:08:54,394
Look how these children of such
a tender age are rallying themselves.

962
01:08:55,228 --> 01:08:57,730
Like Kyojuro...

963
01:08:57,731 --> 01:09:00,108
in order to live up to the Rengoku name...

964
01:09:00,692 --> 01:09:03,528
I will protect them with my life.

965
01:09:16,500 --> 01:09:19,962
<i>She looks as if she's suffering.</i>

966
01:09:20,712 --> 01:09:26,218
<i>The demon named Tamayo, who was working
with the Master, sent over this drug.</i>

967
01:09:26,593 --> 01:09:29,888
<i>I've administered it as she instructed...</i>

968
01:09:31,098 --> 01:09:37,145
<i>but can Nezuko
actually turn back into a human?</i>

969
01:09:37,688 --> 01:09:43,693
<i>If Nezuko does become human again,
Muzan's scheme will collapse.</i>

970
01:09:43,694 --> 01:09:46,153
<i>The dream of the perfect body,</i>

971
01:09:46,154 --> 01:09:50,241
<i>for which he's searched
for more than a thousand years...</i>

972
01:09:50,242 --> 01:09:56,081
<i>his quest to conquer the sun
will be set back to square one.</i>

973
01:09:57,332 --> 01:10:00,751
<i>Throughout all these long years,</i>

974
01:10:00,752 --> 01:10:06,091
<i>Nezuko is the only demon
not to succumb to sunlight.</i>

975
01:10:21,773 --> 01:10:27,738
<i>The words "the final stage"
keep crossing my mind.</i>

976
01:10:30,449 --> 01:10:35,829
<i>And each time, I tremble at my core,
and my heart pounds.</i>

977
01:10:36,913 --> 01:10:41,668
<i>This long battle may finally end tonight.</i>

978
01:10:42,294 --> 01:10:47,424
<i>I never dreamed
that I'd be alive to see it myself.</i>

979
01:10:48,091 --> 01:10:49,717
<i>Tanjiro...</i>

980
01:10:49,718 --> 01:10:50,801
<i>Now that I think of it,</i>

981
01:10:50,802 --> 01:10:55,182
<i>ever since that moment when you
brought your demon sister to me...</i>

982
01:10:55,682 --> 01:11:02,147
<i>a great cogwheel of some kind
seems to have started turning.</i>

983
01:11:02,814 --> 01:11:06,108
<i>If the by-product of all our battles</i>

984
01:11:06,109 --> 01:11:09,154
<i>until now can be likened
to a giant machine...</i>

985
01:11:09,654 --> 01:11:15,911
<i>then inserting you and Nezuko
into it as two small cogs...</i>

986
01:11:16,328 --> 01:11:21,792
<i>is what set the stagnant situation
into motion.</i>

987
01:11:25,045 --> 01:11:27,881
<i>Don't lose, Nezuko!</i>

988
01:11:28,840 --> 01:11:31,218
<i>Don't lose, Tanjiro!</i>

989
01:11:32,511 --> 01:11:35,388
<i>Whatever you do, don't lose!</i>

990
01:11:35,889 --> 01:11:37,224
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

991
01:11:37,808 --> 01:11:38,934
<i>Fire Wheel!</i>

992
01:11:42,062 --> 01:11:45,982
<i>Go! Go! Go! If I can't even sever his arm,
I'll never sever his head!</i>

993
01:11:52,948 --> 01:11:53,949
<i>I severed it!</i>

994
01:11:54,491 --> 01:11:55,866
<i>I was able to dodge his attack, too!</i>

995
01:11:55,867 --> 01:11:58,410
<i>I can do it! I can fight him!</i>

996
01:11:58,411 --> 01:12:00,038
<i>I couldn't go for his head!</i>

997
01:12:00,330 --> 01:12:01,540
<i>But next time...</i>

998
01:12:03,041 --> 01:12:04,208
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

999
01:12:04,209 --> 01:12:05,293
<i>Fake Rainbow!</i>

1000
01:12:21,017 --> 01:12:22,518
<i>Tanjiro...</i>

1001
01:12:22,519 --> 01:12:25,522
<i>You've really honed your techniques.</i>

1002
01:12:26,606 --> 01:12:31,236
<i>It wouldn't be exaggerating to say
that your skills are at Hashira level.</i>

1003
01:12:31,945 --> 01:12:35,991
<i>You can hold your own like this
against Upper Three!</i>

1004
01:12:41,496 --> 01:12:42,747
<i>That day...</i>

1005
01:12:43,456 --> 01:12:45,125
<i>you'd lost all hope in the snow...</i>

1006
01:12:45,876 --> 01:12:48,878
<i>unable to do anything
but bow your head...</i>

1007
01:12:48,879 --> 01:12:52,257
<i>and sob as you begged
for your sister's life.</i>

1008
01:13:00,015 --> 01:13:02,309
<i>But now you can fight.</i>

1009
01:13:03,310 --> 01:13:08,773
<i>To keep from being robbed
of your life and dignity.</i>

1010
01:13:10,192 --> 01:13:15,112
"This boy isn't weak! Don't insult him."

1011
01:13:15,113 --> 01:13:19,075
I admit that Kyojuro
was right in saying that.

1012
01:13:19,659 --> 01:13:22,369
You indeed were not weak.

1013
01:13:22,370 --> 01:13:24,706
Hats off to you!

1014
01:13:27,918 --> 01:13:30,003
<i>Technique Development...</i>

1015
01:13:34,633 --> 01:13:37,385
Well, let's get this party started.

1016
01:13:38,178 --> 01:13:40,639
It's time to have some fun.

1017
01:14:26,810 --> 01:14:27,978
<i>Water Breathing...</i>

1018
01:14:28,561 --> 01:14:29,646
<i>Third Form...</i>

1019
01:14:30,105 --> 01:14:31,189
<i>Flowing Dance!</i>

1020
01:14:32,440 --> 01:14:34,150
The Water Hashira, huh?

1021
01:14:34,609 --> 01:14:36,110
Great...

1022
01:14:36,111 --> 01:14:39,322
It's been 50 years
since I last ran into one!

1023
01:14:46,788 --> 01:14:48,122
<i>Destructive Death...</i>

1024
01:14:48,123 --> 01:14:49,916
<i>Disorder!</i>

1025
01:14:52,127 --> 01:14:54,671
<i>Water Breathing, Eleventh Form...</i>

1026
01:14:55,714 --> 01:14:56,840
<i>Dead Calm!</i>

1027
01:15:02,137 --> 01:15:04,514
I've never seen that move before.

1028
01:15:05,056 --> 01:15:08,852
The Water Hashira I killed before
didn't use it!

1029
01:15:09,769 --> 01:15:11,270
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1030
01:15:11,271 --> 01:15:12,647
<i>Raging Sun!</i>

1031
01:15:14,441 --> 01:15:16,067
<i>He... vanished?</i>

1032
01:15:17,110 --> 01:15:18,111
<i>Behind me?</i>

1033
01:15:18,445 --> 01:15:20,113
<i>Hinokami Kagura, Fake Rain--</i>

1034
01:15:21,323 --> 01:15:24,116
<i>Water Breathing, Second Form...</i>

1035
01:15:24,117 --> 01:15:25,910
<i>Water Wheel!</i>

1036
01:15:38,048 --> 01:15:39,257
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1037
01:15:40,967 --> 01:15:42,051
<i>Flame Dance!</i>

1038
01:15:42,052 --> 01:15:44,262
<i>Destructive Death, Leg Type...</i>

1039
01:15:44,554 --> 01:15:46,389
<i>Crown Splitter!</i>

1040
01:15:47,307 --> 01:15:49,267
<i>I caught it with my sword!</i>

1041
01:15:53,897 --> 01:15:55,189
<i>Did it graze me?</i>

1042
01:15:55,190 --> 01:15:56,398
<i>Just a bit?</i>

1043
01:15:56,399 --> 01:15:57,984
<i>And it's this powerful?</i>

1044
01:16:02,530 --> 01:16:03,782
That's elegant!

1045
01:16:05,909 --> 01:16:07,910
What a polished sword skill that is!

1046
01:16:07,911 --> 01:16:09,453
Magnificent!

1047
01:16:09,454 --> 01:16:10,746
Tell me your name!

1048
01:16:10,747 --> 01:16:12,498
What is your name?

1049
01:16:12,499 --> 01:16:14,084
I want to remember you!

1050
01:16:16,252 --> 01:16:19,005
I don't have a name to divulge to a demon!

1051
01:16:19,339 --> 01:16:22,008
I hate talking, so don't speak to me!

1052
01:16:22,967 --> 01:16:26,888
I see, so you're not into talking?

1053
01:16:27,263 --> 01:16:29,349
I happen to love talking!

1054
01:16:29,641 --> 01:16:31,518
I'm going to keep asking you, then...

1055
01:16:31,976 --> 01:16:33,561
what your name is!

1056
01:16:39,984 --> 01:16:41,568
<i>Destructive Death...</i>

1057
01:16:41,569 --> 01:16:42,987
<i>Leg Type...</i>

1058
01:16:43,279 --> 01:16:45,323
<i>Explosive Flurry!</i>

1059
01:16:58,086 --> 01:16:59,295
Mr. Giyu!

1060
01:17:01,047 --> 01:17:02,339
I see!

1061
01:17:02,340 --> 01:17:05,343
So, his name is Giyu!

1062
01:17:09,180 --> 01:17:10,514
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1063
01:17:10,515 --> 01:17:12,141
<i>Destructive Death...</i>

1064
01:17:12,142 --> 01:17:13,475
<i>Eight-Layered Demon Core!</i>

1065
01:17:13,476 --> 01:17:15,478
<i>Burning Bones, Summer Sun!</i>

1066
01:17:31,244 --> 01:17:33,203
Good moves.

1067
01:17:33,204 --> 01:17:36,708
You did well to train to this level
in such a short time.

1068
01:17:37,041 --> 01:17:38,877
You have my praise.

1069
01:17:39,377 --> 01:17:43,381
Still, Kyojuro did a damn fine job.

1070
01:17:43,798 --> 01:17:49,636
Crumpled on the ground that night,
you were an absolute weakling.

1071
01:17:49,637 --> 01:17:52,140
You were nothing but a weed.

1072
01:17:52,515 --> 01:17:54,183
But what do you know?

1073
01:17:54,184 --> 01:17:56,310
Look at you now!

1074
01:17:56,311 --> 01:17:58,479
Such eye-opening growth!

1075
01:17:58,480 --> 01:18:00,814
I'm purely elated!

1076
01:18:00,815 --> 01:18:02,984
This makes my heart race!

1077
01:18:05,737 --> 01:18:09,866
I'm glad that Kyojuro died that night.

1078
01:18:12,076 --> 01:18:16,164
Otherwise, he might never have gotten
any stronger than he was.

1079
01:18:16,539 --> 01:18:21,628
After all, he did have those lame values,
wanting to remain a human.

1080
01:18:23,171 --> 01:18:24,672
What did you say?

1081
01:18:31,679 --> 01:18:32,889
You...

1082
01:18:33,306 --> 01:18:35,183
don't say another word.

1083
01:18:38,895 --> 01:18:42,148
Don't you dare talk about Mr. Rengoku!

1084
01:18:42,815 --> 01:18:44,107
Why not?

1085
01:18:44,108 --> 01:18:46,402
These are words of praise.

1086
01:18:46,736 --> 01:18:50,239
For you, as well. For Kyojuro, too.

1087
01:18:50,240 --> 01:18:51,573
No, they're not!

1088
01:18:51,574 --> 01:18:53,951
All you're doing is insulting him!

1089
01:18:53,952 --> 01:18:56,370
You're just spitting on him, that's all!

1090
01:18:56,371 --> 01:18:58,540
On everyone!

1091
01:18:59,249 --> 01:19:01,708
You're mistaken, Tanjiro.

1092
01:19:01,709 --> 01:19:03,126
You see...

1093
01:19:03,127 --> 01:19:06,714
the only thing I hate is a weakling.

1094
01:19:07,090 --> 01:19:11,678
I would only spit on a weakling,
no one else.

1095
01:19:12,220 --> 01:19:13,680
That's right.

1096
01:19:14,138 --> 01:19:17,183
The weak make my skin crawl.

1097
01:19:17,559 --> 01:19:19,435
They make me vomit.

1098
01:19:20,186 --> 01:19:24,941
They're weeded out
due to the law of nature, nothing else.

1099
01:19:25,692 --> 01:19:28,820
Everything you just said is wrong!

1100
01:19:32,156 --> 01:19:36,703
Your being here now is proof of that!

1101
01:19:37,579 --> 01:19:40,539
Everyone's a weak infant at birth!

1102
01:19:40,540 --> 01:19:43,501
We can't stay alive
without someone else's help!

1103
01:19:43,918 --> 01:19:46,087
That goes for you, too, Akaza.

1104
01:19:46,963 --> 01:19:49,298
You may not remember it,

1105
01:19:49,299 --> 01:19:50,591
but when you were a baby,

1106
01:19:50,592 --> 01:19:53,344
you were protected
and helped by someone...

1107
01:19:53,970 --> 01:19:56,222
and that's why you're alive now!

1108
01:20:00,560 --> 01:20:03,687
The strong save and protect the weak!

1109
01:20:03,688 --> 01:20:08,985
And the weak become strong and save
and protect those weaker than themselves!

1110
01:20:09,652 --> 01:20:12,238
That's the law of nature!

1111
01:20:12,614 --> 01:20:16,367
Akaza, I won't tolerate
your way of thinking!

1112
01:20:16,826 --> 01:20:20,455
I won't let you have your way anymore!

1113
01:20:25,418 --> 01:20:27,337
<i>I get it now.</i>

1114
01:20:30,381 --> 01:20:34,927
<i>I have a deep-seated aversion to this guy.</i>

1115
01:20:35,595 --> 01:20:39,682
<i>He's stronger, but my revulsion
for him hasn't faded!</i>

1116
01:20:43,978 --> 01:20:45,937
<i>Whatever they do...</i>

1117
01:20:45,938 --> 01:20:48,524
<i>everyone starts out as a baby.</i>

1118
01:20:48,900 --> 01:20:52,278
<i>We learn by getting help
from those around us.</i>

1119
01:20:53,196 --> 01:20:55,906
<i>We are not competing against each other.</i>

1120
01:20:55,907 --> 01:20:59,452
<i>The opponent you're up against
will always be you yourself.</i>

1121
01:20:59,994 --> 01:21:04,457
<i>The important thing is to become
stronger than you were yesterday.</i>

1122
01:21:05,333 --> 01:21:08,752
<i>If you can keep that up
for a decade or two,</i>

1123
01:21:08,753 --> 01:21:10,796
<i>that would be commendable.</i>

1124
01:21:10,797 --> 01:21:12,340
<i>And then...</i>

1125
01:21:12,715 --> 01:21:15,843
<i>it'll be you helping out others this time.</i>

1126
01:21:23,309 --> 01:21:26,979
<i>What was that? He just swung at nothing.</i>

1127
01:21:32,443 --> 01:21:33,861
Tanjiro...

1128
01:21:34,946 --> 01:21:37,573
You repulse me after all.

1129
01:21:38,741 --> 01:21:40,993
<i>Destructive Death, Crushing Type...</i>

1130
01:21:41,703 --> 01:21:43,830
<i>Ten Thousand Leaves Flashing Willow!</i>

1131
01:21:46,958 --> 01:21:48,709
<i>So fast! Insanely fast!</i>

1132
01:21:48,710 --> 01:21:49,876
<i>No...</i>

1133
01:21:49,877 --> 01:21:51,586
<i>it's not really about speed!</i>

1134
01:21:51,587 --> 01:21:54,214
<i>This sensation, this precision...</i>

1135
01:21:54,215 --> 01:21:55,466
<i>this is...</i>

1136
01:21:59,762 --> 01:22:01,638
<i>Destructive Death, Leg Type...</i>

1137
01:22:01,639 --> 01:22:02,765
<i>From below!</i>

1138
01:22:05,268 --> 01:22:07,311
<i>Flying Planet Thousand Wheels!</i>

1139
01:22:13,192 --> 01:22:16,153
<i>Even if I manage to predict
his movements and intercept the attack,</i>

1140
01:22:16,154 --> 01:22:18,990
<i>the impact is so strong,
I can't escape unscathed!</i>

1141
01:22:19,282 --> 01:22:21,241
<i>A technique of unparalleled precision!</i>

1142
01:22:21,242 --> 01:22:24,412
<i>He can pierce through any opening
with the accuracy of a compass!</i>

1143
01:22:27,415 --> 01:22:29,624
<i>It's like there are magnets
pulling his blows</i>

1144
01:22:29,625 --> 01:22:31,836
<i>straight to the human body's vitals!</i>

1145
01:22:32,336 --> 01:22:33,336
<i>But how?</i>

1146
01:22:33,337 --> 01:22:34,422
<i>What is this?</i>

1147
01:22:35,256 --> 01:22:37,883
<i>What's causing them
to be drawn in like this?</i>

1148
01:22:37,884 --> 01:22:39,719
<i>Try to remember! Think!</i>

1149
01:22:41,137 --> 01:22:42,805
<i>There's got to be something!</i>

1150
01:22:43,097 --> 01:22:44,931
<i>If you can find a clue
in what Akaza has said</i>

1151
01:22:44,932 --> 01:22:46,309
<i>and done until now...</i>

1152
01:22:49,812 --> 01:22:50,980
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1153
01:22:51,272 --> 01:22:52,732
<i>Solar Heat Haze!</i>

1154
01:23:03,493 --> 01:23:05,453
Interesting technique!

1155
01:23:05,828 --> 01:23:07,204
I know I dodged it for sure,

1156
01:23:07,205 --> 01:23:09,498
but then it looked like
the blade extended.

1157
01:23:09,499 --> 01:23:11,792
I don't know what kind
of swing you put on it...

1158
01:23:11,793 --> 01:23:16,380
but the tip of your blade wavered
like it was in a heat haze! I'm intrigued!

1159
01:23:27,558 --> 01:23:29,143
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1160
01:23:29,894 --> 01:23:30,895
<i>Dance!</i>

1161
01:23:33,147 --> 01:23:34,482
<i>Oh, crap!</i>

1162
01:23:35,525 --> 01:23:36,818
<i>He's going to break it!</i>

1163
01:23:41,614 --> 01:23:43,324
That's a good head-butt!

1164
01:23:44,784 --> 01:23:47,411
<i>Let go! Let go! Let go!</i>

1165
01:23:48,913 --> 01:23:52,750
<i>No good! He's not letting go!</i>

1166
01:24:04,679 --> 01:24:06,097
Mr. Giyu!

1167
01:24:09,934 --> 01:24:12,061
I'm furious right now.

1168
01:24:12,478 --> 01:24:15,606
Because my back is absolutely killing me.

1169
01:24:15,940 --> 01:24:18,776
How dare you hurl me all that distance...

1170
01:24:19,151 --> 01:24:21,612
Upper Three?

1171
01:24:23,906 --> 01:24:25,323
<i>Personally...</i>

1172
01:24:25,324 --> 01:24:28,368
<i>I'd rather not draw my sword
if I can help it...</i>

1173
01:24:28,369 --> 01:24:33,124
<i>and I don't enjoy sparring
random passersby for amusement.</i>

1174
01:24:33,958 --> 01:24:35,834
<i>But right now...</i>

1175
01:24:35,835 --> 01:24:37,586
<i>I can feel that facing a strong opponent</i>

1176
01:24:37,587 --> 01:24:39,379
<i>who overwhelms me for
the first time in a while...</i>

1177
01:24:39,380 --> 01:24:43,634
<i>has sharply honed my senses
in a short span of time.</i>

1178
01:24:44,510 --> 01:24:47,262
<i>My dormant senses
have been rudely awakened</i>

1179
01:24:47,263 --> 01:24:49,055
<i>and are dragging me forward.</i>

1180
01:24:49,056 --> 01:24:51,725
<i>To the place where the strong one stands.</i>

1181
01:24:51,726 --> 01:24:55,021
<i>I understand now
how much it expands one's potential...</i>

1182
01:24:55,438 --> 01:24:58,190
<i>to fight to the death...</i>

1183
01:24:58,524 --> 01:25:00,526
<i>until the very last moment.</i>

1184
01:25:03,905 --> 01:25:05,489
Mr. Giyu...

1185
01:25:22,381 --> 01:25:24,883
<i>A mark appeared. His speed...</i>

1186
01:25:24,884 --> 01:25:26,344
Has increased!

1187
01:25:31,307 --> 01:25:32,808
<i>Water Breathing, Fourth Form...</i>

1188
01:25:33,309 --> 01:25:34,393
<i>Striking Tide!</i>

1189
01:25:48,866 --> 01:25:50,534
<i>So fast! Both of them!</i>

1190
01:25:50,868 --> 01:25:53,329
<i>But in response
to Mr. Giyu's speed boost...</i>

1191
01:25:53,621 --> 01:25:55,706
<i>Akaza adapted instantly!</i>

1192
01:25:58,167 --> 01:26:00,461
Is that the best you can do?

1193
01:26:09,553 --> 01:26:10,888
More!

1194
01:26:11,305 --> 01:26:13,182
Strike more attacks on me!

1195
01:26:42,294 --> 01:26:43,546
<i>Tenth Form...</i>

1196
01:26:44,130 --> 01:26:45,798
<i>Constant Flux!</i>

1197
01:27:02,815 --> 01:27:04,190
<i>Seventh Form...</i>

1198
01:27:04,191 --> 01:27:05,985
<i>Drop Ripple Thrust!</i>

1199
01:27:06,277 --> 01:27:07,319
<i>Destructive Death...</i>

1200
01:27:07,820 --> 01:27:09,488
<i>Disorder!</i>

1201
01:27:20,082 --> 01:27:21,249
Mr. Giyu!

1202
01:27:21,250 --> 01:27:22,334
Akaza!

1203
01:27:24,712 --> 01:27:26,130
<i>Calm down!</i>

1204
01:27:29,884 --> 01:27:32,218
<i>Think. Don't panic.</i>

1205
01:27:32,219 --> 01:27:35,181
<i>Don't relinquish your mind
whatever you do!</i>

1206
01:27:36,432 --> 01:27:39,894
<i>Why are Akaza's attacks
as accurate as magnets?</i>

1207
01:27:40,978 --> 01:27:44,815
<i>Why does he unfailingly react to attacks
from behind and in his blind spots?</i>

1208
01:27:45,941 --> 01:27:47,276
<i>Think!</i>

1209
01:27:51,739 --> 01:27:54,200
<i>Your fighting spirit
has been honed to the hilt.</i>

1210
01:27:54,533 --> 01:27:57,453
<i>It's close to the realm of the highest.</i>

1211
01:27:59,872 --> 01:28:02,082
<i>Akaza used the words "fighting spirit"...</i>

1212
01:28:02,083 --> 01:28:05,461
<i>during his battle with Mr. Rengoku.</i>

1213
01:28:07,088 --> 01:28:08,922
<i>What's "fighting spirit"?</i>

1214
01:28:08,923 --> 01:28:11,717
<i>As I can sense all kinds of things
through scent...</i>

1215
01:28:12,343 --> 01:28:15,012
<i>Akaza seems to sense things
through fighting spirit.</i>

1216
01:28:29,276 --> 01:28:33,614
<i>It tingles, you know.
Where the enemy is aiming at.</i>

1217
01:28:33,989 --> 01:28:37,117
<i>So, that's how you knew
that Gyutaro was attacking you.</i>

1218
01:28:37,118 --> 01:28:39,411
<i>Even though it was from behind!
That was awesome!</i>

1219
01:28:41,497 --> 01:28:44,208
<i>Well, my skin is tougher
than most people's!</i>

1220
01:28:44,625 --> 01:28:46,042
<i>Whether it's from behind or not,</i>

1221
01:28:46,043 --> 01:28:49,379
<i>if someone is looking at me,
I can tell that they're looking!</i>

1222
01:28:49,380 --> 01:28:51,090
<i>Can you show me?</i>

1223
01:28:52,174 --> 01:28:53,259
<i>Sure thing!</i>

1224
01:28:58,430 --> 01:29:00,014
<i>You're looking
at my right shoulder, aren't you?</i>

1225
01:29:00,015 --> 01:29:01,684
<i>Wow! You got it!</i>

1226
01:29:02,518 --> 01:29:04,561
<i>I can tell right away
especially if someone is looking at me</i>

1227
01:29:04,562 --> 01:29:06,272
<i>with killing intent!</i>

1228
01:29:06,772 --> 01:29:09,691
<i>Since anyone who could harm me
is bad news.</i>

1229
01:29:09,692 --> 01:29:13,904
<i>Killing intent feels like it's stabbing me
through the skin.</i>

1230
01:29:14,947 --> 01:29:16,072
<i>That's right,</i>

1231
01:29:16,073 --> 01:29:21,537
<i>Inosuke could sense the invisible
through his honed sense of touch.</i>

1232
01:29:22,246 --> 01:29:25,541
<i>What else did we talk about...</i>

1233
01:29:26,083 --> 01:29:27,501
<i>that day?</i>

1234
01:29:28,002 --> 01:29:29,377
<i>But the thing is,</i>

1235
01:29:29,378 --> 01:29:34,090
<i>it's hard to catch onto someone
without any killing intent or hostility.</i>

1236
01:29:34,091 --> 01:29:36,010
<i>- That tiny hag!
- Huh?</i>

1237
01:29:36,886 --> 01:29:38,386
<i>The old hag from the house</i>

1238
01:29:38,387 --> 01:29:41,140
<i>with the wisteria family
crest was a real terror.</i>

1239
01:29:41,724 --> 01:29:43,559
<i>Before I knew it...</i>

1240
01:29:45,519 --> 01:29:48,355
<i>she'd be sitting behind me
holding rice balls!</i>

1241
01:29:49,815 --> 01:29:52,609
<i>You shouldn't call her a "hag"!
She's an elderly lady!</i>

1242
01:29:52,610 --> 01:29:54,903
- <i>Elderly hag!
- Hey!</i>

1243
01:29:54,904 --> 01:29:56,779
<i>That got me thinking.</i>

1244
01:29:56,780 --> 01:29:59,908
<i>If I can sneak up without letting out
any killing intent, I won't be detected!</i>

1245
01:29:59,909 --> 01:30:02,745
<i>Then there wouldn't be anyone
I couldn't kill!</i>

1246
01:30:03,996 --> 01:30:05,121
<i>Hmm,</i>

1247
01:30:05,122 --> 01:30:10,418
<i>but isn't that because she didn't have
any intention of harming you?</i>

1248
01:30:10,419 --> 01:30:11,628
<i>I think that killing a demon</i>

1249
01:30:11,629 --> 01:30:14,924
<i>without emitting any killing intent
would be impossible.</i>

1250
01:30:16,884 --> 01:30:19,093
<i>Well, you're probably right.</i>

1251
01:30:19,094 --> 01:30:22,055
<i>A half-hearted strike
without any killing intent</i>

1252
01:30:22,056 --> 01:30:23,514
<i>couldn't cut through...</i>

1253
01:30:23,515 --> 01:30:25,434
<i>a demon's hard neck.</i>

1254
01:30:26,560 --> 01:30:31,982
<i>It was just a casual conversation,
but I think he was on to something bigger.</i>

1255
01:30:33,692 --> 01:30:38,905
<i>What is it that Akaza supposedly senses
as fighting spirit?</i>

1256
01:30:38,906 --> 01:30:40,907
<i>Is it not killing intent?</i>

1257
01:30:40,908 --> 01:30:42,575
<i>Is it the will to fight?</i>

1258
01:30:42,576 --> 01:30:45,871
<i>The amount of time spent training?
Or maybe the quantity?</i>

1259
01:30:46,705 --> 01:30:49,583
<i>Is it like the way I can anticipate
movements through scent?</i>

1260
01:30:51,377 --> 01:30:55,673
<i>Isn't there any way
that I can disrupt Akaza's compass?</i>

1261
01:31:05,683 --> 01:31:06,766
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1262
01:31:06,767 --> 01:31:07,851
<i>Dance!</i>

1263
01:31:10,312 --> 01:31:12,772
Your torso is wide open...

1264
01:31:12,773 --> 01:31:14,566
Tanjiro!

1265
01:31:17,695 --> 01:31:18,696
<i>It's coming!</i>

1266
01:31:31,959 --> 01:31:34,335
<i>Fighting spirit, magnet...</i>

1267
01:31:34,336 --> 01:31:35,629
<i>compass...</i>

1268
01:31:36,338 --> 01:31:38,382
<i>perception, killing intent...</i>

1269
01:31:38,799 --> 01:31:39,800
<i>the impossible...</i>

1270
01:31:40,676 --> 01:31:43,137
<i>the realm of the highest...</i>

1271
01:31:43,679 --> 01:31:44,930
<i>I see.</i>

1272
01:31:46,890 --> 01:31:47,933
<i>That's what it is.</i>

1273
01:32:05,617 --> 01:32:06,868
<i>Father...</i>

1274
01:32:06,869 --> 01:32:08,578
<i>When you perform
the Hinokami Kagura dance,</i>

1275
01:32:08,579 --> 01:32:10,331
<i>what are you thinking?</i>

1276
01:32:11,332 --> 01:32:14,877
<i>If it's too tiring for you, Father,
I'll take your place starting next year.</i>

1277
01:32:15,502 --> 01:32:17,838
<i>I'm worried about your health.</i>

1278
01:32:19,298 --> 01:32:21,633
<i>Thank you, Tanjiro.</i>

1279
01:32:21,967 --> 01:32:27,598
<i>But I haven't found the Kagura
to be tiring for the last few years.</i>

1280
01:32:28,599 --> 01:32:30,141
<i>I don't know how to explain it,</i>

1281
01:32:30,142 --> 01:32:33,645
<i>but back when I first learned
it from your grandfather...</i>

1282
01:32:33,937 --> 01:32:37,690
<i>even though I was younger, healthier
and stronger than I am now,</i>

1283
01:32:37,691 --> 01:32:41,111
<i>I kept losing my breath,
and it was so hard.</i>

1284
01:32:44,573 --> 01:32:47,325
<i>The Kagura performed
at the start of each year</i>

1285
01:32:47,326 --> 01:32:50,204
<i>was passed down through
the Kamado Family lineage.</i>

1286
01:32:50,662 --> 01:32:53,831
<i>It was a grueling event
that went on interminably</i>

1287
01:32:53,832 --> 01:32:55,918
<i>from sunset to dawn the next morning.</i>

1288
01:32:56,668 --> 01:33:00,338
<i>There are 12 different styles,
which are repeated until daybreak...</i>

1289
01:33:00,339 --> 01:33:04,009
<i>hundreds, thousands,
tens of thousands of times.</i>

1290
01:33:06,678 --> 01:33:10,891
<i>I think I was simply making
too many wasteful motions.</i>

1291
01:33:11,266 --> 01:33:14,018
<i>The important thing
is to breathe correctly</i>

1292
01:33:14,019 --> 01:33:15,521
<i>and to move correctly.</i>

1293
01:33:16,271 --> 01:33:20,900
<i>To produce maximum strength
with minimal action.</i>

1294
01:33:20,901 --> 01:33:27,366
<i>By doing that, your mind
gradually becomes transparent.</i>

1295
01:33:27,991 --> 01:33:29,493
<i>Transparent?</i>

1296
01:33:30,452 --> 01:33:32,161
<i>At first, you need to memorize</i>

1297
01:33:32,162 --> 01:33:37,626
<i>all of the movements
and acquire a feel for it.</i>

1298
01:33:38,043 --> 01:33:39,544
<i>You open up all five senses</i>

1299
01:33:39,545 --> 01:33:45,384
<i>and become aware of the shape
of your own body vessel by vessel.</i>

1300
01:33:47,428 --> 01:33:50,179
<i>That was the truly strenuous part.</i>

1301
01:33:50,180 --> 01:33:52,682
<i>All you can think is that,
even if you go on struggling,</i>

1302
01:33:52,683 --> 01:33:55,352
<i>you'll never succeed.</i>

1303
01:33:56,103 --> 01:33:59,397
<i>After you've learned all these things
and absorbed them,</i>

1304
01:33:59,398 --> 01:34:02,650
<i>you remove what you don't need.</i>

1305
01:34:02,651 --> 01:34:06,404
<i>Only leave what you need
for that movement...</i>

1306
01:34:06,405 --> 01:34:08,115
<i>and close the rest.</i>

1307
01:34:09,366 --> 01:34:10,701
<i>Close the rest?</i>

1308
01:34:11,118 --> 01:34:15,998
<i>You know people often close their eyes
when they're trying to hear better?</i>

1309
01:34:16,373 --> 01:34:23,255
<i>Just like that, you pick out the things
you need the most in that moment.</i>

1310
01:34:23,672 --> 01:34:26,466
<i>Eventually, you'll be able
to open and close</i>

1311
01:34:26,467 --> 01:34:28,342
<i>the vessels and muscles in your body...</i>

1312
01:34:28,343 --> 01:34:33,265
<i>as quickly and easily
as if you were blinking.</i>

1313
01:34:34,600 --> 01:34:39,521
<i>When that happens, a path
illuminated by a bright light will open.</i>

1314
01:34:41,440 --> 01:34:43,816
<i>When your mind becomes transparent,</i>

1315
01:34:43,817 --> 01:34:47,445
<i>you can start to see
the Transparent World.</i>

1316
01:34:47,446 --> 01:34:48,988
<i>But this is a domain...</i>

1317
01:34:48,989 --> 01:34:51,657
<i>you can only reach after
you've struggled and suffered,</i>

1318
01:34:51,658 --> 01:34:54,286
<i>pushing yourself to your limits.</i>

1319
01:34:54,786 --> 01:34:57,039
<i>Do you think I can get there, too?</i>

1320
01:34:57,831 --> 01:35:01,668
<i>If you keep working at it tirelessly, yes.</i>

1321
01:35:02,002 --> 01:35:03,920
<i>Here, all done.</i>

1322
01:35:03,921 --> 01:35:05,297
<i>Thanks!</i>

1323
01:35:09,218 --> 01:35:11,637
<i>Ten days before my father passed away...</i>

1324
01:35:12,012 --> 01:35:16,934
<i>a bear attacked and devoured people
on a neighboring mountain.</i>

1325
01:35:17,476 --> 01:35:23,065
<i>We lit bonfires around the house
and put up ropes with bells on them.</i>

1326
01:35:41,416 --> 01:35:43,085
<i>Tanjiro...</i>

1327
01:35:47,339 --> 01:35:48,590
<i>Yes?</i>

1328
01:35:49,841 --> 01:35:51,843
<i>Come with me.</i>

1329
01:36:40,142 --> 01:36:47,024
<i>I'm sorry that you're hungry,
but I won't let you come any closer.</i>

1330
01:36:47,691 --> 01:36:50,610
<i>If anyone tries to harm my family,</i>

1331
01:36:50,611 --> 01:36:53,863
<i>I will show no mercy no matter
how many of them there are.</i>

1332
01:36:53,864 --> 01:36:56,116
<i>Disregard my warning...</i>

1333
01:36:59,453 --> 01:37:02,956
<i>and I will take your life.</i>

1334
01:37:13,717 --> 01:37:17,219
<i>The bear's head,
as thick as a human torso,</i>

1335
01:37:17,220 --> 01:37:20,641
<i>dropped to the ground
with the sound of the bells.</i>

1336
01:37:22,517 --> 01:37:24,268
<i>My eyes couldn't follow it,</i>

1337
01:37:24,269 --> 01:37:29,232
<i>but I think my father slashed it
twice in the blink of an eye.</i>

1338
01:37:31,443 --> 01:37:32,860
<i>Otherwise,</i>

1339
01:37:32,861 --> 01:37:36,657
<i>it wouldn't have been possible to chop
off its head with an axe of that breadth.</i>

1340
01:37:37,574 --> 01:37:40,452
<i>My father's scent
never wavered in the least.</i>

1341
01:37:40,911 --> 01:37:43,621
<i>Before and after beheading the bear,
he emitted no fear,</i>

1342
01:37:43,622 --> 01:37:47,417
<i>no uncertainty, no killing intent.</i>

1343
01:37:54,383 --> 01:37:56,385
<i>Did you get a good look?</i>

1344
01:37:57,511 --> 01:38:00,430
<i>Don't forget what you just saw.</i>

1345
01:38:03,266 --> 01:38:07,229
<i>My father wasn't one
to flaunt his strength for no reason.</i>

1346
01:38:07,562 --> 01:38:09,439
<i>I realized this later on.</i>

1347
01:38:09,981 --> 01:38:11,399
<i>That was...</i>

1348
01:38:11,400 --> 01:38:13,944
<i>him letting me watch and learn.</i>

1349
01:38:14,653 --> 01:38:18,239
<i>So that I could learn from observing
the body movements of my father...</i>

1350
01:38:18,240 --> 01:38:20,242
<i>who could see the Transparent World.</i>

1351
01:38:22,244 --> 01:38:26,832
<i>Just like Father, Grandfather
and Great-Grandfather...</i>

1352
01:38:27,249 --> 01:38:29,209
<i>must've all done before me.</i>

1353
01:38:31,086 --> 01:38:33,546
<i>You must never give up.</i>

1354
01:38:33,547 --> 01:38:36,091
<i>Just keep thinking.</i>

1355
01:38:36,466 --> 01:38:39,594
<i>You can break through
any wall eventually...</i>

1356
01:38:39,928 --> 01:38:42,055
<i>with tireless effort.</i>

1357
01:38:43,807 --> 01:38:45,683
<i>I know, Father.</i>

1358
01:38:45,684 --> 01:38:47,144
<i>That's why...</i>

1359
01:38:47,769 --> 01:38:51,857
<i>I was able to dodge
Akaza's magnetic, inescapable blow!</i>

1360
01:38:55,068 --> 01:38:59,948
<i>That was probably a lethal blow
meant to kill me once and for all.</i>

1361
01:39:00,365 --> 01:39:02,659
<i>When I was alternating moves
with Mr. Giyu...</i>

1362
01:39:03,118 --> 01:39:05,077
<i>I could take momentary breaks...</i>

1363
01:39:05,078 --> 01:39:09,040
<i>and he protected me
from the potentially mortal blows!</i>

1364
01:39:09,583 --> 01:39:13,336
<i>But in that instant,
even Mr. Giyu couldn't make it in time!</i>

1365
01:39:14,629 --> 01:39:17,673
<i>However, for some reason...</i>

1366
01:39:17,674 --> 01:39:20,177
<i>in that moment, it didn't feel impossible.</i>

1367
01:39:20,844 --> 01:39:22,929
<i>I felt it for just a split second.</i>

1368
01:39:23,305 --> 01:39:25,557
<i>I was able to enter it
for just a split second.</i>

1369
01:39:26,683 --> 01:39:28,101
<i>That world.</i>

1370
01:39:32,397 --> 01:39:34,524
<i>The Transparent World.</i>

1371
01:39:36,985 --> 01:39:39,988
<i>His body looked transparent.</i>

1372
01:39:41,198 --> 01:39:44,910
<i>The same as when Hantengu
was hiding inside his own heart.</i>

1373
01:39:45,577 --> 01:39:48,079
<i>I don't know if I was able
to see him or if I smelled him.</i>

1374
01:39:53,043 --> 01:39:54,418
<i>Dodge.</i>

1375
01:39:54,419 --> 01:39:57,714
<i>I focused on just that,
and I closed off all other senses.</i>

1376
01:39:58,006 --> 01:40:01,760
<i>My body moved faster
than it ever had before.</i>

1377
01:40:03,345 --> 01:40:04,887
<i>When I'm able to enter
the Transparent World</i>

1378
01:40:04,888 --> 01:40:06,639
<i>that Father told me about,</i>

1379
01:40:06,640 --> 01:40:07,973
<i>my ability to predict movements,</i>

1380
01:40:07,974 --> 01:40:10,602
<i>and the speed of my
attacks improve dramatically!</i>

1381
01:40:12,270 --> 01:40:14,146
<i>I can see my opponent's lungs moving...</i>

1382
01:40:14,147 --> 01:40:17,107
<i>his vessels flowing and contracting
through his body.</i>

1383
01:40:17,108 --> 01:40:19,276
<i>I can even see my own muscles contracting.</i>

1384
01:40:19,277 --> 01:40:20,403
<i>Faster...</i>

1385
01:40:20,779 --> 01:40:22,405
<i>and even clearer!</i>

1386
01:40:26,451 --> 01:40:28,702
<i>I may be able to close off
the fighting spirit</i>

1387
01:40:28,703 --> 01:40:30,746
<i>that Akaza is likely detecting...</i>

1388
01:40:30,747 --> 01:40:33,166
<i>and aim for his head!</i>

1389
01:40:45,971 --> 01:40:47,264
<i>See it.</i>

1390
01:40:47,722 --> 01:40:48,807
<i>See it!</i>

1391
01:40:52,269 --> 01:40:55,772
It looks like you've thrown
every last Water Form you have at me.

1392
01:40:56,606 --> 01:40:59,526
That's enough, Giyu.

1393
01:40:59,860 --> 01:41:01,652
Let's end this!

1394
01:41:01,653 --> 01:41:04,322
I'm impressed that you held out this long!

1395
01:41:06,324 --> 01:41:07,742
<i>No way!</i>

1396
01:41:08,201 --> 01:41:10,287
<i>In the middle of the downswing...</i>

1397
01:41:12,038 --> 01:41:13,582
<i>he snapped it...</i>

1398
01:41:15,417 --> 01:41:17,419
<i>from the side!</i>

1399
01:41:17,711 --> 01:41:18,795
Farewell.

1400
01:41:49,242 --> 01:41:52,578
<i>He slashed his arm amidst his strike
and stopped him.</i>

1401
01:41:52,579 --> 01:41:54,538
<i>The sound of his breathing is different.</i>

1402
01:41:54,539 --> 01:41:56,583
<i>His hair and eyes, too!</i>

1403
01:41:57,459 --> 01:41:59,711
<i>I've been saved by Tanjiro.</i>

1404
01:42:01,379 --> 01:42:04,924
<i>Every cell in my body,
right down to the tips of my hairs,</i>

1405
01:42:04,925 --> 01:42:08,428
<i>is telling me to kill him this instant.</i>

1406
01:42:09,804 --> 01:42:12,766
<i>He's undergone some kind of change.</i>

1407
01:42:14,225 --> 01:42:15,602
<i>He's dangerous.</i>

1408
01:42:17,312 --> 01:42:19,981
<i>He's focusing on Tanjiro.</i>

1409
01:42:20,565 --> 01:42:22,108
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

1410
01:42:26,488 --> 01:42:29,240
<i>Technique Development Final Form...</i>

1411
01:42:29,991 --> 01:42:32,744
<i>Blue Silver Chaotic Afterglow!</i>

1412
01:42:35,705 --> 01:42:38,040
<i>He's boosting his attack speed again!</i>

1413
01:42:38,041 --> 01:42:40,168
<i>The force is increasing!</i>

1414
01:42:40,460 --> 01:42:41,878
<i>Can I take it...</i>

1415
01:42:42,379 --> 01:42:43,546
<i>with Dead Calm?</i>

1416
01:43:05,652 --> 01:43:08,071
<i>This is what Father was talking about.</i>

1417
01:43:08,780 --> 01:43:09,990
<i>This is...</i>

1418
01:43:10,657 --> 01:43:12,367
<i>the Transparent World!</i>

1419
01:43:20,875 --> 01:43:22,251
<i>What's this?</i>

1420
01:43:22,252 --> 01:43:23,586
<i>It's so strange.</i>

1421
01:43:23,962 --> 01:43:26,381
<i>Time is passing by so slowly.</i>

1422
01:43:28,591 --> 01:43:29,759
<i>No...</i>

1423
01:43:30,343 --> 01:43:33,430
<i>is it just that the movements look slow?</i>

1424
01:43:39,477 --> 01:43:41,020
<i>Unavoidable.</i>

1425
01:43:41,021 --> 01:43:44,399
<i>He made 100 blows almost simultaneously.</i>

1426
01:43:44,899 --> 01:43:49,279
<i>I couldn't block them all
even with Dead Calm.</i>

1427
01:43:50,989 --> 01:43:52,614
That was impressive.

1428
01:43:52,615 --> 01:43:55,410
As expected, you survived.

1429
01:43:55,744 --> 01:43:59,164
It looks like you managed
to evade any fatal blows.

1430
01:43:59,456 --> 01:44:03,292
No need for you to die
like Kyojuro and Tanjiro.

1431
01:44:03,293 --> 01:44:06,671
You should become a demon, too, Giyu!

1432
01:44:08,256 --> 01:44:09,923
<i>He hasn't noticed!</i>

1433
01:44:09,924 --> 01:44:12,009
<i>That Tanjiro's behind him!</i>

1434
01:44:12,010 --> 01:44:16,930
<i>Does he have no presence?
This is...</i>

1435
01:44:16,931 --> 01:44:19,516
<i>Tanjiro, slash him!</i>

1436
01:44:19,517 --> 01:44:21,394
<i>If you can still move, go for it!</i>

1437
01:44:22,020 --> 01:44:23,687
<i>Before he notices you!</i>

1438
01:44:23,688 --> 01:44:25,190
<i>Take his head!</i>

1439
01:44:25,690 --> 01:44:29,069
Akaza! I'm going to behead you now!

1440
01:44:35,200 --> 01:44:37,994
<i>He gave himself away?</i>

1441
01:44:38,369 --> 01:44:39,788
<i>He's alive?</i>

1442
01:44:40,580 --> 01:44:44,501
<i>I never dreamed
that after that attack, he'd still...</i>

1443
01:44:44,834 --> 01:44:46,752
<i>No, it's not a big deal!</i>

1444
01:44:46,753 --> 01:44:51,382
<i>My Destructive Death, Compass Needle
can detect any attack!</i>

1445
01:44:51,716 --> 01:44:54,593
<i>The stronger
my opponent's fighting spirit is,</i>

1446
01:44:54,594 --> 01:44:57,514
<i>the greater my Compass Needle's reaction!</i>

1447
01:45:01,184 --> 01:45:03,019
<i>What is that?</i>

1448
01:45:03,561 --> 01:45:05,980
<i>What's that bizarre presence?</i>

1449
01:45:06,523 --> 01:45:09,525
<i>It's like he's turned into
some other creature!</i>

1450
01:45:09,526 --> 01:45:11,236
<i>This guy...</i>

1451
01:45:12,320 --> 01:45:14,154
<i>His fighting spirit's gone!</i>

1452
01:45:14,155 --> 01:45:15,824
<i>He has no fighting spirit!</i>

1453
01:45:16,116 --> 01:45:17,700
<i>Calm down!</i>

1454
01:45:18,076 --> 01:45:19,327
<i>He's coming!</i>

1455
01:45:25,500 --> 01:45:27,252
<i>Hinokami Kagura...</i>

1456
01:45:27,710 --> 01:45:29,963
<i>Setting Sun Transformation.</i>

1457
01:45:51,484 --> 01:45:54,404
<i>Im... possible!</i>

1458
01:46:01,161 --> 01:46:03,328
<i>In the last several hundred years,</i>

1459
01:46:03,329 --> 01:46:07,417
<i>I've never once seen a human
without any fighting spirit!</i>

1460
01:46:07,876 --> 01:46:11,129
<i>Even newborns have traces of it!</i>

1461
01:46:11,588 --> 01:46:18,052
<i>And yet, in that instant,
his fighting spirit completely vanished!</i>

1462
01:46:21,431 --> 01:46:26,059
<i>It was like I was facing
an anomaly that shouldn't be there...</i>

1463
01:46:26,060 --> 01:46:28,770
<i>and my senses were thrown into confusion.</i>

1464
01:46:28,771 --> 01:46:32,192
<i>My Compass Needle detected nothing.</i>

1465
01:46:34,068 --> 01:46:36,778
<i>But that's not the issue here!</i>

1466
01:46:36,779 --> 01:46:38,405
<i>On the battlefield,</i>

1467
01:46:38,406 --> 01:46:43,619
<i>you must instantly understand
the unforeseen and the unexpected...</i>

1468
01:46:43,620 --> 01:46:45,871
<i>and deal with them then and there!</i>

1469
01:46:45,872 --> 01:46:48,208
<i>I have the ability to do that!</i>

1470
01:46:49,334 --> 01:46:51,753
<i>Or so I thought.</i>

1471
01:46:52,712 --> 01:46:55,881
<i>But during this short battle,</i>

1472
01:46:55,882 --> 01:47:00,136
<i>he grasped something
and surpassed my speed!</i>

1473
01:47:00,511 --> 01:47:04,681
<i>The very best of martial arts,
honed over several centuries...</i>

1474
01:47:04,682 --> 01:47:07,352
<i>He shattered them with a head-on attack!</i>

1475
01:47:08,019 --> 01:47:12,731
<i>There was no hatred or rage in his eyes...</i>

1476
01:47:12,732 --> 01:47:15,610
<i>no killing intent
or fighting spirit, either!</i>

1477
01:47:16,152 --> 01:47:21,198
<i>Most likely, those eyes
had perceived what I've been seeking...</i>

1478
01:47:21,199 --> 01:47:23,785
<i>the realm of the highest!</i>

1479
01:47:25,036 --> 01:47:28,373
<i>None other than the selfless state.</i>

1480
01:47:29,666 --> 01:47:34,795
<i>I've had a vague sense
that this state existed...</i>

1481
01:47:34,796 --> 01:47:39,259
<i>but I've never yet managed to attain it.</i>

1482
01:47:48,685 --> 01:47:50,143
<i>I'm not done yet!</i>

1483
01:47:50,144 --> 01:47:52,104
<i>I can still fight!</i>

1484
01:47:52,105 --> 01:47:54,857
<i>I can still become stronger!</i>

1485
01:48:00,989 --> 01:48:04,200
<i>Is he trying to... reattach his head?</i>

1486
01:48:13,167 --> 01:48:14,836
<i>I can't let it end!</i>

1487
01:48:16,921 --> 01:48:19,382
<i>Not here!</i>

1488
01:48:21,592 --> 01:48:23,803
<i>I'm going to get stronger!</i>

1489
01:48:26,347 --> 01:48:29,684
<i>I've got to become stronger
than anyone else!</i>

1490
01:48:30,059 --> 01:48:31,936
<i>Stronger!</i>

1491
01:48:33,938 --> 01:48:37,483
<i>Even stronger.</i>

1492
01:48:46,701 --> 01:48:48,160
<i>It disintegrated!</i>

1493
01:48:48,161 --> 01:48:49,620
<i>It's over now!</i>

1494
01:48:51,372 --> 01:48:52,832
<i>We won!</i>

1495
01:48:57,712 --> 01:48:59,714
<i>I'm so dizzy...</i>

1496
01:49:01,299 --> 01:49:03,009
<i>My muscles are cramping.</i>

1497
01:49:03,343 --> 01:49:05,720
<i>My body's reached its limit!</i>

1498
01:49:07,972 --> 01:49:09,599
Are you all right? Tanjiro--

1499
01:49:11,642 --> 01:49:14,145
<i>His body isn't disintegrating!</i>

1500
01:49:14,520 --> 01:49:15,896
<i>Does this...</i>

1501
01:49:15,897 --> 01:49:17,857
- <i>Does this mean...</i>
- Tan--

1502
01:49:29,452 --> 01:49:30,786
<i>He's still moving!</i>

1503
01:49:30,787 --> 01:49:32,497
<i>His body's not crumbling!</i>

1504
01:49:32,789 --> 01:49:35,208
<i>The severed part is closing up!</i>

1505
01:49:38,252 --> 01:49:39,837
<i>So dizzy...</i>

1506
01:49:52,725 --> 01:49:55,352
<i>No way... No way!</i>

1507
01:49:55,353 --> 01:49:57,647
<i>Even after I cut off his head,
he still won't die?</i>

1508
01:49:57,980 --> 01:49:59,606
<i>Is there some kind of condition to meet?</i>

1509
01:49:59,607 --> 01:50:01,317
<i>Like with Gyutaro and Daki?</i>

1510
01:50:01,651 --> 01:50:02,652
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

1511
01:50:02,985 --> 01:50:04,821
<i>His head crumbled and disappeared!</i>

1512
01:50:05,196 --> 01:50:07,156
<i>He's trying to change right now!</i>

1513
01:50:07,490 --> 01:50:08,532
<i>Akaza's also...</i>

1514
01:50:08,533 --> 01:50:10,243
<i>trying to evolve into something else!</i>

1515
01:50:17,083 --> 01:50:21,212
<i>He's trying to become like Muzan,
whose head is not his weak point!</i>

1516
01:50:22,130 --> 01:50:23,964
This battle isn't over!

1517
01:50:23,965 --> 01:50:26,466
The fight is still--

1518
01:50:26,467 --> 01:50:27,718
Tanjiro!

1519
01:50:28,052 --> 01:50:29,636
<i>He fainted!</i>

1520
01:50:29,637 --> 01:50:30,972
<i>Well, of course!</i>

1521
01:50:31,305 --> 01:50:33,558
<i>He's long since blown past his limit!</i>

1522
01:50:43,151 --> 01:50:44,569
<i>Water Breathing...</i>

1523
01:50:45,069 --> 01:50:46,404
<i>Fourth Form...</i>

1524
01:50:49,240 --> 01:50:50,575
<i>Striking Tide!</i>

1525
01:50:55,663 --> 01:50:57,081
<i>He's regenerating!</i>

1526
01:50:57,415 --> 01:51:01,085
<i>Even after losing his head,
his speed is...</i>

1527
01:51:24,692 --> 01:51:27,277
<i>I can't hear a thing out of my left ear.</i>

1528
01:51:27,278 --> 01:51:29,739
<i>I have no sensation in my right hand.</i>

1529
01:51:30,698 --> 01:51:34,285
<i>I can still grip with it,
but I don't know how useful I'll be.</i>

1530
01:51:43,085 --> 01:51:44,378
Hold it!

1531
01:51:45,046 --> 01:51:46,214
I...

1532
01:51:46,964 --> 01:51:48,256
I'm...

1533
01:51:48,257 --> 01:51:50,509
still alive!

1534
01:51:50,510 --> 01:51:54,847
If you want to kill Tanjiro,
you'll have to defeat me first!

1535
01:51:59,185 --> 01:52:01,436
<i>An indomitable spirit...</i>

1536
01:52:01,437 --> 01:52:05,858
<i>It will never bend
no matter what crisis it finds itself in.</i>

1537
01:52:06,734 --> 01:52:09,444
<i>We're not samurai.</i>

1538
01:52:09,445 --> 01:52:11,488
<i>We don't carry swords.</i>

1539
01:52:11,489 --> 01:52:15,159
<i>But we always carry swords in our hearts.</i>

1540
01:52:16,285 --> 01:52:19,455
<i>But we always carry swords in our hearts.</i>

1541
01:52:20,414 --> 01:52:21,790
<i>All we use...</i>

1542
01:52:21,791 --> 01:52:23,834
<i>are our own fists.</i>

1543
01:52:25,628 --> 01:52:27,504
<i>You are...</i>

1544
01:52:27,505 --> 01:52:28,965
<i>an eyesore!</i>

1545
01:52:39,267 --> 01:52:40,726
<i>Please stop.</i>

1546
01:52:46,941 --> 01:52:48,442
<i>Who is that?</i>

1547
01:52:54,073 --> 01:52:55,865
<i>Mr. Hakuji...</i>

1548
01:52:55,866 --> 01:52:58,077
<i>Please stop already!</i>

1549
01:53:00,913 --> 01:53:02,581
<i>Let go.</i>

1550
01:53:02,582 --> 01:53:04,834
<i>Let go of my hand!</i>

1551
01:53:05,209 --> 01:53:07,253
<i>Who the hell are you?</i>

1552
01:53:08,963 --> 01:53:11,757
<i>Let's stop this right now!</i>

1553
01:53:12,216 --> 01:53:14,969
<i>Let's go to the other side!</i>

1554
01:53:15,428 --> 01:53:17,012
<i>I can't.</i>

1555
01:53:17,013 --> 01:53:20,391
<i>I've got to kill those two!</i>

1556
01:53:21,851 --> 01:53:23,811
<i>Why is that?</i>

1557
01:53:24,478 --> 01:53:27,898
<i>I've got to become stronger!</i>

1558
01:53:28,357 --> 01:53:31,277
<i>I'll kill anyone who gets in my way!</i>

1559
01:53:32,278 --> 01:53:34,447
<i>Why is that?</i>

1560
01:53:35,072 --> 01:53:38,409
<i>Why do you wish to become stronger?</i>

1561
01:53:39,702 --> 01:53:41,329
<i>Because...</i>

1562
01:53:41,871 --> 01:53:44,164
<i>unless I'm strong...</i>

1563
01:53:44,165 --> 01:53:47,793
<i>I can't bring it back home
for him anymore!</i>

1564
01:53:49,420 --> 01:53:52,298
<i>The medicine for my dad!</i>

1565
01:53:53,799 --> 01:53:56,177
<i>I've got to become stronger...</i>

1566
01:53:58,346 --> 01:54:01,974
<i>or I won't be able to run off
with the wallet I stole!</i>

1567
01:54:03,517 --> 01:54:05,268
<i>I've got to become stronger...</i>

1568
01:54:05,269 --> 01:54:07,980
<i>or I won't be able to defeat them
when they retaliate!</i>

1569
01:54:08,981 --> 01:54:10,899
<i>I've got to become stronger...</i>

1570
01:54:10,900 --> 01:54:14,820
<i>or I'll get caught by the magistrate
and lashed as punishment!</i>

1571
01:54:17,907 --> 01:54:22,078
<i>You've already got three tattoos
for pickpocketing on both arms!</i>

1572
01:54:22,453 --> 01:54:24,955
<i>Next time,
we're going to chop off your hands!</i>

1573
01:54:32,755 --> 01:54:35,006
<i>Lower your head! Kneel more!</i>

1574
01:54:35,007 --> 01:54:37,051
<i>Go ahead and chop them off!</i>

1575
01:54:37,426 --> 01:54:40,095
<i>Even if you chop both hands off,
I'll still have my feet!</i>

1576
01:54:40,096 --> 01:54:42,472
<i>I'll use my feet to steal!</i>

1577
01:54:42,473 --> 01:54:45,810
<i>Regardless,
I'm not gonna get caught next time!</i>

1578
01:54:47,812 --> 01:54:51,315
<i>A repeat offender
at the tender age of 11...</i>

1579
01:54:51,774 --> 01:54:53,942
<i>And all this bravado
after taking 100 lashes</i>

1580
01:54:53,943 --> 01:54:56,821
<i>that would make grown men faint!</i>

1581
01:54:57,780 --> 01:54:59,531
<i>You're a demon child!</i>

1582
01:54:59,532 --> 01:55:01,783
<i>Call me whatever you want!</i>

1583
01:55:01,784 --> 01:55:04,494
<i>That's right, I'm a demon child!</i>

1584
01:55:04,495 --> 01:55:07,789
<i>They say I already had teeth
when I was born after all!</i>

1585
01:55:07,790 --> 01:55:08,873
<i>Insolent boy!</i>

1586
01:55:08,874 --> 01:55:10,125
<i>You little punk!</i>

1587
01:55:10,126 --> 01:55:13,212
<i>"Demon child" is fine by me, you bastards!</i>

1588
01:55:14,004 --> 01:55:20,010
{\an8}SOUTH TOWN MAGISTRATE'S OFFICE

1589
01:55:22,763 --> 01:55:24,181
<i>Hakuji!</i>

1590
01:55:24,557 --> 01:55:26,182
<i>Hakuji!</i>

1591
01:55:26,183 --> 01:55:32,313
<i>Your father heard that you'd been caught
stealing again, and he hanged himself!</i>

1592
01:55:32,314 --> 01:55:35,443
<i>He's dead!</i>

1593
01:55:40,072 --> 01:55:41,866
<i>Dear Hakuji...</i>

1594
01:55:43,159 --> 01:55:45,244
<i>Live an honest life.</i>

1595
01:55:45,911 --> 01:55:48,038
<i>You can still start over.</i>

1596
01:55:55,296 --> 01:55:57,380
<i>So, the poor...</i>

1597
01:55:57,381 --> 01:56:00,634
<i>aren't even allowed to live?</i>

1598
01:56:05,431 --> 01:56:06,891
<i>Dad...</i>

1599
01:56:09,226 --> 01:56:12,897
<i>To hell with this rotten world!</i>

1600
01:56:15,983 --> 01:56:18,109
<i>Every last one of you...</i>

1601
01:56:18,110 --> 01:56:20,070
<i>You can all just die and rot in hell!</i>

1602
01:56:23,824 --> 01:56:26,869
<i>Why do scumbags like these get to live...</i>

1603
01:56:27,244 --> 01:56:30,456
<i>when my dad had to go and die?</i>

1604
01:56:30,998 --> 01:56:33,082
<i>You weren't causing any trouble!</i>

1605
01:56:33,083 --> 01:56:35,461
<i>Why would you apologize?</i>

1606
01:56:35,795 --> 01:56:38,589
<i>You didn't do anything wrong, Dad!</i>

1607
01:56:41,550 --> 01:56:45,512
<i>I didn't even mind
getting lashed for stealing!</i>

1608
01:56:45,513 --> 01:56:49,349
<i>Even if they beat me black-and-blue
or broke my bones...</i>

1609
01:56:49,350 --> 01:56:51,227
<i>I could take it all for you, Dad!</i>

1610
01:56:51,519 --> 01:56:52,644
<i>For centuries, even!</i>

1611
01:56:52,645 --> 01:56:53,978
<i>Repent!</i>

1612
01:56:53,979 --> 01:56:55,356
<i>Earn an honest living!</i>

1613
01:56:56,232 --> 01:56:59,108
<i>Why don't you shut up, scum?</i>

1614
01:56:59,109 --> 01:57:00,986
<i>I don't have enough money.</i>

1615
01:57:01,362 --> 01:57:04,240
<i>Medicine costs a lot!</i>

1616
01:57:05,407 --> 01:57:09,495
<i>My dad was getting thinner and thinner.</i>

1617
01:57:10,120 --> 01:57:13,374
<i>The bones were starting
to jut out of his back.</i>

1618
01:57:13,749 --> 01:57:17,044
<i>I want him to have something
more nutritious to eat!</i>

1619
01:57:19,213 --> 01:57:21,799
<i>I would've been happy to die...</i>

1620
01:57:24,218 --> 01:57:26,345
<i>if it were for my dad's sake!</i>

1621
01:57:32,393 --> 01:57:33,769
<i>For my...</i>

1622
01:57:34,562 --> 01:57:36,188
<i>dad's sake!</i>

1623
01:57:44,530 --> 01:57:47,408
<i>Oh, wow! That is impressive!</i>

1624
01:57:47,825 --> 01:57:51,452
<i>I was called here because someone said
a child was about to be killed,</i>

1625
01:57:51,453 --> 01:57:55,290
<i>but you've flattened seven grown-ups
with your bare fists.</i>

1626
01:57:55,291 --> 01:57:57,750
<i>You've got talent, kid!</i>

1627
01:57:57,751 --> 01:58:01,421
<i>To take on grown-ups unarmed
and still win!</i>

1628
01:58:01,422 --> 01:58:04,383
<i>That's what I like to see!</i>

1629
01:58:06,176 --> 01:58:08,428
<i>Who the hell is that?</i>

1630
01:58:08,429 --> 01:58:10,764
<i>What am I seeing?</i>

1631
01:58:11,599 --> 01:58:13,892
<i>Are these my memories?</i>

1632
01:58:13,893 --> 01:58:16,019
<i>Wanna join my dojo?</i>

1633
01:58:16,020 --> 01:58:18,354
<i>I don't have any students.</i>

1634
01:58:18,355 --> 01:58:20,315
<i>Shut up, you stupid old geezer!</i>

1635
01:58:20,316 --> 01:58:21,858
<i>I'll kill you!</i>

1636
01:58:21,859 --> 01:58:23,611
<i>Those tattoos tell me...</i>

1637
01:58:23,944 --> 01:58:26,112
<i>that you're a criminal from Edo, right?</i>

1638
01:58:26,113 --> 01:58:30,658
<i>So, you've been banished from Edo,
and you ended up here?</i>

1639
01:58:30,659 --> 01:58:32,952
<i>So, what if I did?</i>

1640
01:58:32,953 --> 01:58:35,288
<i>That's none of your business!</i>

1641
01:58:35,289 --> 01:58:39,376
<i>Yes! First off,
time to be reborn, young man.</i>

1642
01:58:39,877 --> 01:58:41,337
<i>All right, bring it!</i>

1643
01:58:42,338 --> 01:58:43,339
<i>You...</i>

1644
01:58:43,839 --> 01:58:45,758
<i>drop dead, you old fart!</i>

1645
01:59:04,276 --> 01:59:05,610
{\an8}SORYU DOJO

1646
01:59:05,611 --> 01:59:08,571
<i>Well, you sure are durable.</i>

1647
01:59:08,572 --> 01:59:13,618
<i>After that pummeling I gave you,
you came to in less than an hour.</i>

1648
01:59:13,619 --> 01:59:15,453
<i>I'm Keizo.</i>

1649
01:59:15,454 --> 01:59:18,081
<i>I run a dojo where I teach</i>

1650
01:59:18,082 --> 01:59:20,042
<i>the Soryu Style of
fighting with bare hands.</i>

1651
01:59:20,542 --> 01:59:23,586
<i>But I don't have a single student...</i>

1652
01:59:23,587 --> 01:59:27,883
<i>so I earn a living
as a handyman, doing odd jobs.</i>

1653
01:59:30,219 --> 01:59:35,473
<i>The first thing I want you to do
is look after my sickly daughter.</i>

1654
01:59:35,474 --> 01:59:39,561
<i>Since I have work,
I'd like to leave her in your care.</i>

1655
01:59:40,020 --> 01:59:44,316
<i>My wife drowned herself the other day
due to nursing fatigue.</i>

1656
01:59:45,484 --> 01:59:47,945
<i>I'm really at my wits' end
as you can see.</i>

1657
01:59:51,490 --> 01:59:54,242
<i>Really, thanks to my incompetence...</i>

1658
01:59:54,243 --> 01:59:57,413
<i>both my wife and daughter have suffered.</i>

1659
01:59:59,540 --> 02:00:01,666
<i>Are you sure you want
to leave a criminal like me</i>

1660
02:00:01,667 --> 02:00:04,920
<i>alone with your daughter?</i>

1661
02:00:06,422 --> 02:00:10,718
<i>I pummeled
the criminal out of you earlier...</i>

1662
02:00:11,051 --> 02:00:12,302
<i>so it's fine.</i>

1663
02:00:15,305 --> 02:00:17,057
<i>They're alike.</i>

1664
02:00:24,648 --> 02:00:26,358
<i>I get it now.</i>

1665
02:00:28,068 --> 02:00:31,320
<i>The reason you repulsed me...</i>

1666
02:00:31,321 --> 02:00:36,201
<i>was because you reminded me
of my worthless past.</i>

1667
02:00:40,581 --> 02:00:43,292
<i>This is my daughter, Koyuki.</i>

1668
02:00:45,919 --> 02:00:48,380
<i>My worthless past...</i>

1669
02:00:51,759 --> 02:00:54,386
<i>Worthless...</i>

1670
02:01:02,227 --> 02:01:03,811
<i>Hakuji...</i>

1671
02:01:03,812 --> 02:01:05,814
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

1672
02:01:07,399 --> 02:01:08,984
<i>How are you, Koyuki?</i>

1673
02:01:11,070 --> 02:01:12,905
<i>Is it okay for you to be up?</i>

1674
02:01:13,530 --> 02:01:15,240
<i>Yes.</i>

1675
02:01:15,616 --> 02:01:18,702
<i>You're right, you have more color
than you did this morning.</i>

1676
02:01:19,286 --> 02:01:20,746
<i>Do you feel a bit better?</i>

1677
02:01:21,121 --> 02:01:22,456
<i>Yes.</i>

1678
02:01:23,707 --> 02:01:25,959
<i>Oh, him?</i>

1679
02:01:26,293 --> 02:01:28,170
<i>His name is...</i>

1680
02:01:28,629 --> 02:01:31,422
<i>I've asked him numerous times,
but he won't tell me.</i>

1681
02:01:31,423 --> 02:01:33,634
<i>Hey, don't just stand out there!</i>

1682
02:01:35,135 --> 02:01:36,595
<i>Have a seat here.</i>

1683
02:01:38,222 --> 02:01:41,600
<i>All right, get it out of him
before I get home!</i>

1684
02:01:52,736 --> 02:01:53,946
<i>Um...</i>

1685
02:01:54,613 --> 02:01:57,908
<i>Y-Your face...</i>

1686
02:01:58,367 --> 02:01:59,743
<i>You're hurt.</i>

1687
02:02:00,119 --> 02:02:01,578
<i>Are you all right?</i>

1688
02:02:05,040 --> 02:02:06,999
<i>I'll heal you for sure.</i>

1689
02:02:07,000 --> 02:02:08,543
<i>I'll save you...</i>

1690
02:02:08,544 --> 02:02:09,962
<i>protect you...</i>

1691
02:02:10,879 --> 02:02:15,591
<i>All I ever did in my worthless life...</i>

1692
02:02:15,592 --> 02:02:17,970
<i>was spew baseless lies.</i>

1693
02:02:34,194 --> 02:02:36,321
<i>Thank you.</i>

1694
02:02:37,322 --> 02:02:40,032
<i>You don't have to thank me
every single time.</i>

1695
02:02:40,033 --> 02:02:42,369
<i>Don't worry about it. Go to sleep.</i>

1696
02:02:43,620 --> 02:02:45,621
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

1697
02:02:45,622 --> 02:02:47,582
<i>for causing you trouble.</i>

1698
02:02:47,583 --> 02:02:49,585
<i>I said it was all right.</i>

1699
02:02:51,712 --> 02:02:54,339
<i>Do you want me to shut this?</i>

1700
02:02:54,882 --> 02:02:56,424
<i>No...</i>

1701
02:02:56,425 --> 02:02:59,094
<i>you can leave it as is.</i>

1702
02:03:00,596 --> 02:03:03,849
<i>Koyuki was truly delicate and frail.</i>

1703
02:03:04,892 --> 02:03:07,143
<i>I had to stay with her all night...</i>

1704
02:03:07,144 --> 02:03:10,731
<i>change the towels
for her forehead and her nightgown...</i>

1705
02:03:11,023 --> 02:03:13,316
<i>and give her water frequently.</i>

1706
02:03:13,317 --> 02:03:18,238
<i>When she needed to use the restroom,
it was a given I had to carry her there.</i>

1707
02:03:21,575 --> 02:03:25,536
<i>I'd already been taking care of my dad,</i>

1708
02:03:25,537 --> 02:03:29,123
<i>and since I had extraordinary
physical endurance,</i>

1709
02:03:29,124 --> 02:03:31,752
<i>it really wasn't a hardship for me.</i>

1710
02:03:35,964 --> 02:03:38,592
<i>Sorry to make you do this every day.</i>

1711
02:03:45,307 --> 02:03:50,395
<i>Why do people suffering from illness
always say they're sorry?</i>

1712
02:03:51,063 --> 02:03:53,731
<i>"Sorry to put you through all this."</i>

1713
02:03:53,732 --> 02:03:56,902
<i>"Sorry the sound
of my coughing bothers you."</i>

1714
02:03:57,277 --> 02:04:00,614
<i>"Sorry I can't work like I should."</i>

1715
02:04:02,491 --> 02:04:05,451
<i>They'd rather care
for themselves if they could.</i>

1716
02:04:05,452 --> 02:04:07,620
<i>And it's not like they can
just stop coughing.</i>

1717
02:04:07,621 --> 02:04:10,415
<i>If they could breathe normally,
they would.</i>

1718
02:04:11,124 --> 02:04:15,545
<i>They're the ones
who must be suffering the most.</i>

1719
02:04:18,257 --> 02:04:20,800
<i>Sorry again.</i>

1720
02:04:20,801 --> 02:04:25,471
<i>You can't even train because of me...</i>

1721
02:04:25,472 --> 02:04:28,058
<i>and you can't go play.</i>

1722
02:04:28,684 --> 02:04:32,646
<i>I don't want to go play. I never have.</i>

1723
02:04:33,188 --> 02:04:37,442
<i>I train in my spare time here and there,
so don't worry about it.</i>

1724
02:04:38,694 --> 02:04:40,195
<i>But...</i>

1725
02:04:40,612 --> 02:04:44,074
<i>you must want a change
of scenery sometimes.</i>

1726
02:04:44,449 --> 02:04:48,035
<i>I hear they're setting off
fireworks tonight...</i>

1727
02:04:48,036 --> 02:04:50,080
<i>so, please, go.</i>

1728
02:04:51,081 --> 02:04:52,915
<i>Right.</i>

1729
02:04:52,916 --> 02:04:55,334
<i>If you're not dizzy by then,</i>

1730
02:04:55,335 --> 02:04:58,839
<i>shall I carry you on my back
to just before the bridge?</i>

1731
02:04:59,172 --> 02:05:00,215
<i>What?</i>

1732
02:05:03,885 --> 02:05:05,845
<i>Even if you can't go today,</i>

1733
02:05:05,846 --> 02:05:09,015
<i>they'll be setting off fireworks
next year and the year after,</i>

1734
02:05:09,016 --> 02:05:11,393
<i>so we can just go then.</i>

1735
02:05:19,943 --> 02:05:23,529
<i>The only time I found nursing
to be a hassle...</i>

1736
02:05:23,530 --> 02:05:29,119
<i>was when Koyuki started sobbing
while we were talking.</i>

1737
02:05:29,619 --> 02:05:32,663
<i>I'm sure she was feeling down,
sick in bed...</i>

1738
02:05:32,664 --> 02:05:36,418
<i>but it made me uncomfortable
when she cried.</i>

1739
02:05:37,627 --> 02:05:40,130
{\an8}SORYU

1740
02:05:51,558 --> 02:05:53,435
<i>Oh, I get it.</i>

1741
02:05:53,894 --> 02:05:55,895
<i>This is the character
for the "haku" in your name?</i>

1742
02:05:55,896 --> 02:05:57,938
<i>It's the same as the "koma" in komainu.</i>

1743
02:05:57,939 --> 02:05:59,440
<i>That makes sense.</i>

1744
02:05:59,441 --> 02:06:01,901
<i>Just as I thought, you're the same as me.</i>

1745
02:06:01,902 --> 02:06:05,112
<i>You can't get by
unless you have something to protect.</i>

1746
02:06:05,113 --> 02:06:09,076
<i>Just like those komainu,
the dogs who guard the shrines.</i>

1747
02:06:13,789 --> 02:06:16,832
<i>The reason why the master owned
all this land and the dojo...</i>

1748
02:06:16,833 --> 02:06:20,212
<i>despite not being a samurai or anything...</i>

1749
02:06:20,504 --> 02:06:24,173
<i>was because he'd rescued
an elderly man from bandits,</i>

1750
02:06:24,174 --> 02:06:27,885
<i>who, greatly moved
by his Soryu Style moves,</i>

1751
02:06:27,886 --> 02:06:33,767
<i>left him his land and dojo,
for which he had no heirs.</i>

1752
02:06:36,186 --> 02:06:39,397
<i>But that didn't sit well
with those who wanted</i>

1753
02:06:39,398 --> 02:06:42,734
<i>to have that land and dojo for themselves.</i>

1754
02:06:43,026 --> 02:06:48,740
<i>The kenjutsu dojo next door
started harassing the Soryu Dojo.</i>

1755
02:06:49,783 --> 02:06:54,913
<i>Because of that, the Soryu Dojo
couldn't get any new students.</i>

1756
02:07:01,920 --> 02:07:04,548
<i>But thanks to my training there...</i>

1757
02:07:04,840 --> 02:07:06,174
<i>and my caring for Koyuki...</i>

1758
02:07:08,009 --> 02:07:11,471
<i>my heart found salvation.</i>

1759
02:07:30,198 --> 02:07:31,824
<i>Three years went by...</i>

1760
02:07:31,825 --> 02:07:34,744
<i>and I turned 18.</i>

1761
02:07:35,328 --> 02:07:37,246
<i>Koyuki was 16.</i>

1762
02:07:37,247 --> 02:07:39,666
<i>She was almost never bedridden anymore...</i>

1763
02:07:39,958 --> 02:07:43,003
<i>and could now live a normal life.</i>

1764
02:07:47,007 --> 02:07:48,090
<i>Hakuji...</i>

1765
02:07:48,091 --> 02:07:49,342
<i>Got a second?</i>

1766
02:07:49,926 --> 02:07:51,261
<i>Sure!</i>

1767
02:07:52,721 --> 02:07:53,929
<i>So...</i>

1768
02:07:53,930 --> 02:07:57,642
<i>will you take over this dojo
for me, Hakuji?</i>

1769
02:07:58,018 --> 02:08:01,521
<i>Koyuki says she likes you, too.</i>

1770
02:08:02,397 --> 02:08:03,648
<i>Huh?</i>

1771
02:08:11,156 --> 02:08:14,992
<i>My future as someone
with the tattoos of a criminal...</i>

1772
02:08:14,993 --> 02:08:18,163
<i>wasn't something that I could picture.</i>

1773
02:08:19,289 --> 02:08:26,171
<i>Much less a future with someone
who feels fond of a person like me.</i>

1774
02:08:27,631 --> 02:08:31,675
<i>Could it be that, just like my dad said...</i>

1775
02:08:31,676 --> 02:08:35,680
<i>I would be able to lead
an honest life now?</i>

1776
02:08:36,348 --> 02:08:40,768
<i>The faint hope
of starting all over in life...</i>

1777
02:08:40,769 --> 02:08:45,190
<i>began to swell uncontrollably.</i>

1778
02:08:50,737 --> 02:08:52,822
<i>At that moment...</i>

1779
02:08:53,281 --> 02:08:58,702
<i>I had no inkling that the two people
I wanted to protect with my life...</i>

1780
02:08:58,703 --> 02:09:01,456
<i>would be poisoned to death.</i>

1781
02:09:06,294 --> 02:09:10,215
<i>I went to Edo to visit my dad's grave.</i>

1782
02:09:10,590 --> 02:09:13,969
<i>I wanted to let him know
that I was getting married.</i>

1783
02:09:23,061 --> 02:09:26,731
<i>Though I returned to the dojo
before the sun went down...</i>

1784
02:09:30,235 --> 02:09:33,071
<i>I felt nauseous even before
I heard about it.</i>

1785
02:09:33,697 --> 02:09:36,407
<i>My diaphragm seized up...</i>

1786
02:09:36,408 --> 02:09:39,828
<i>and I had goosebumps
from an ominous premonition.</i>

1787
02:09:42,247 --> 02:09:44,332
<i>Someone put poison in the well!</i>

1788
02:09:45,208 --> 02:09:48,752
<i>Because they could never beat you
or Mr. Keizo head-on...</i>

1789
02:09:48,753 --> 02:09:50,964
<i>they did this horrible thing!</i>

1790
02:09:51,298 --> 02:09:53,757
<i>Atrocious! It's unthinkable!</i>

1791
02:09:53,758 --> 02:09:56,177
<i>They even killed Koyuki!</i>

1792
02:09:58,930 --> 02:10:04,226
<i>When my loved ones
find themselves in danger...</i>

1793
02:10:04,227 --> 02:10:06,354
<i>I'm never nearby.</i>

1794
02:10:15,488 --> 02:10:18,992
<i>Even though I'd promised her...</i>

1795
02:10:20,660 --> 02:10:23,622
<i>Are you sure you're fine with me?</i>

1796
02:10:25,457 --> 02:10:32,172
<i>Do you remember when we were children,
and we talked about seeing the fireworks?</i>

1797
02:10:32,547 --> 02:10:34,757
<i>Huh? No...</i>

1798
02:10:34,758 --> 02:10:36,635
<i>Uh...</i>

1799
02:10:37,969 --> 02:10:44,726
<i>Thanks to those little chats we had,
Mr. Hakuji, I felt joy many times.</i>

1800
02:10:47,020 --> 02:10:50,314
<i>You said that even if we couldn't see
the fireworks this year...</i>

1801
02:10:50,315 --> 02:10:56,320
<i>we could just go next year
or the year after that.</i>

1802
02:10:56,321 --> 02:10:59,865
<i>I could never imagine a future</i>

1803
02:10:59,866 --> 02:11:04,871
<i>in which I'd still be alive
next year or the year after that.</i>

1804
02:11:06,081 --> 02:11:08,083
<i>Neither could my mother.</i>

1805
02:11:08,416 --> 02:11:12,336
<i>I think that's why she killed herself...</i>

1806
02:11:12,337 --> 02:11:15,756
<i>because she didn't want to see me die.</i>

1807
02:11:15,757 --> 02:11:21,221
<i>I could tell that my father
had given up, too, deep down inside.</i>

1808
02:11:21,888 --> 02:11:24,766
<i>Because I was so weak.</i>

1809
02:11:25,809 --> 02:11:31,106
<i>But you were able
to see my future, Mr. Hakuji.</i>

1810
02:11:31,773 --> 02:11:38,446
<i>You talked about next year and the year
after that as if it were perfectly normal.</i>

1811
02:11:39,155 --> 02:11:41,783
<i>That really made me happy!</i>

1812
02:11:52,836 --> 02:11:56,339
<i>You're the one for me, Mr. Hakuji.</i>

1813
02:11:57,882 --> 02:11:59,509
<i>Will you...</i>

1814
02:11:59,926 --> 02:12:02,387
<i>be my husband?</i>

1815
02:12:10,395 --> 02:12:11,521
<i>Yes.</i>

1816
02:12:12,063 --> 02:12:14,816
<i>I'm going to become stronger
than anyone else...</i>

1817
02:12:15,191 --> 02:12:17,819
<i>and protect you for the rest of my life.</i>

1818
02:12:22,198 --> 02:12:23,867
<i>In the end...</i>

1819
02:12:24,325 --> 02:12:29,581
<i>it was all talk, and I was never able
to see a single thing through to the end.</i>

1820
02:12:41,926 --> 02:12:43,553
<i>What do you want?</i>

1821
02:12:44,888 --> 02:12:46,638
<i>How impolite!</i>

1822
02:12:46,639 --> 02:12:47,931
<i>You bastard...</i>

1823
02:12:47,932 --> 02:12:49,434
<i>from Soryu!</i>

1824
02:13:12,874 --> 02:13:14,333
<i>After the father
and daughter of the Soryu Dojo</i>

1825
02:13:14,334 --> 02:13:16,084
<i>were murdered by poison,</i>

1826
02:13:16,085 --> 02:13:20,965
<i>one of the surviving students
attacked the neighboring kenjutsu dojo...</i>

1827
02:13:21,257 --> 02:13:24,009
<i>killing 67 people!</i>

1828
02:13:24,010 --> 02:13:27,847
<i>He shattered their skulls and crushed
their organs with his bare hands!</i>

1829
02:13:28,431 --> 02:13:32,810
<i>Not only did he smash and mangle
most of the bodies beyond recognition,</i>

1830
02:13:32,811 --> 02:13:35,729
<i>they're all missing a significant
amount of body parts!</i>

1831
02:13:35,730 --> 02:13:38,982
<i>The walls and ceilings are strewn
with jaws, brains and eyeballs...</i>

1832
02:13:38,983 --> 02:13:44,404
<i>as well as limbs and organs,
making for a hellish sight!</i>

1833
02:13:44,405 --> 02:13:47,742
<i>The murderer was no ordinary human!</i>

1834
02:14:10,640 --> 02:14:14,476
<i>So, I hear a huge commotion
about a demon sighting</i>

1835
02:14:14,477 --> 02:14:17,355
<i>where I never sent one.</i>

1836
02:14:17,772 --> 02:14:20,399
<i>And now that I've come
to see for myself...</i>

1837
02:14:20,400 --> 02:14:23,318
<i>I find that it was a mere human.</i>

1838
02:14:23,319 --> 02:14:26,405
<i>What a letdown.</i>

1839
02:14:26,406 --> 02:14:28,199
<i>Move it.</i>

1840
02:14:28,533 --> 02:14:29,617
<i>I'll kill you!</i>

1841
02:14:34,747 --> 02:14:39,794
<i>I'm thinking of creating
around 12 powerful demons.</i>

1842
02:14:40,378 --> 02:14:45,633
<i>I wonder if you can withstand
the amount of blood I'm going to give you.</i>

1843
02:14:47,010 --> 02:14:48,553
<i>Don't...</i>

1844
02:14:50,763 --> 02:14:52,222
<i>Don't...</i>

1845
02:14:52,223 --> 02:14:54,725
<i>care anymore...</i>

1846
02:14:54,726 --> 02:14:58,187
<i>about anything...</i>

1847
02:15:12,827 --> 02:15:14,954
<i>After turning into a demon,
I lost my memories...</i>

1848
02:15:16,080 --> 02:15:19,334
<i>and once again, I began to seek power!</i>

1849
02:15:34,557 --> 02:15:35,933
<i>More!</i>

1850
02:15:35,934 --> 02:15:37,977
<i>Show me more of what you've got!</i>

1851
02:15:42,106 --> 02:15:45,108
<i>Even though I no longer...</i>

1852
02:15:45,109 --> 02:15:48,655
<i>had a single thing left
that I wanted to protect.</i>

1853
02:15:50,990 --> 02:15:53,785
<i>Even though it wasn't
as if I wanted to live in a world...</i>

1854
02:15:54,285 --> 02:15:57,789
<i>without my family.</i>

1855
02:16:00,625 --> 02:16:05,546
<i>For over a century, I committed
senseless massacres over and over.</i>

1856
02:16:06,798 --> 02:16:11,552
<i>What an absolutely pathetic, absurd...</i>

1857
02:16:12,804 --> 02:16:15,431
<i>and worthless past.</i>

1858
02:16:20,645 --> 02:16:26,192
<i>Even if I die, I can't go
where the other three are.</i>

1859
02:16:27,610 --> 02:16:30,488
<i>Damn you for making me remember...</i>

1860
02:16:30,863 --> 02:16:32,532
<i>that past of mine!</i>

1861
02:16:34,367 --> 02:16:36,535
<i>Damn humans!</i>

1862
02:16:36,536 --> 02:16:39,622
<i>Such delicate, fragile weaklings!</i>

1863
02:16:40,540 --> 02:16:42,582
<i>They die too easily!</i>

1864
02:16:42,583 --> 02:16:44,168
<i>They break!</i>

1865
02:16:44,544 --> 02:16:47,296
<i>They vanish into thin air!</i>

1866
02:16:50,091 --> 02:16:51,883
<i>He's still not dead!</i>

1867
02:16:51,884 --> 02:16:54,387
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

1868
02:16:55,013 --> 02:16:57,557
<i>I have to kill him right now!</i>

1869
02:16:58,725 --> 02:17:02,854
<i>If we let him regenerate now,
we're done for!</i>

1870
02:17:08,901 --> 02:17:11,529
I blacked out!
In the middle of the battle!

1871
02:17:13,573 --> 02:17:14,865
His head!

1872
02:17:14,866 --> 02:17:17,201
His head's starting to regenerate!

1873
02:17:18,870 --> 02:17:21,205
But I chopped it off!

1874
02:17:27,128 --> 02:17:29,380
<i>Destructive Death, Annihilation Type!</i>

1875
02:17:30,256 --> 02:17:32,258
Stop it!

1876
02:17:32,592 --> 02:17:35,219
<i>That kid! He can still move?</i>

1877
02:17:35,636 --> 02:17:37,554
<i>I'll behead you as many times as it takes!</i>

1878
02:17:37,555 --> 02:17:39,973
<i>We're going to win!
Mr. Giyu and I together!</i>

1879
02:17:39,974 --> 02:17:41,809
<i>We're beating Akaza!</i>

1880
02:17:44,854 --> 02:17:46,355
<i>My sword!</i>

1881
02:17:47,982 --> 02:17:49,901
<i>It slipped out of his hands!</i>

1882
02:17:51,152 --> 02:17:52,737
<i>My grip!</i>

1883
02:18:01,704 --> 02:18:03,498
<i>Time to be reborn...</i>

1884
02:18:04,582 --> 02:18:06,042
<i>young man.</i>

1885
02:18:08,669 --> 02:18:11,297
<i>I despise weaklings!</i>

1886
02:18:13,132 --> 02:18:14,925
<i>Weaklings...</i>

1887
02:18:14,926 --> 02:18:17,719
<i>They pour poison into a well...</i>

1888
02:18:17,720 --> 02:18:20,181
<i>instead of fighting fair and square!</i>

1889
02:18:20,848 --> 02:18:22,892
<i>They're atrocious!</i>

1890
02:18:23,601 --> 02:18:27,646
<i>The weak have no patience!</i>

1891
02:18:27,647 --> 02:18:30,650
<i>They get desperate too soon!</i>

1892
02:18:32,110 --> 02:18:35,655
<i>I killed people with my fists
meant for protection!</i>

1893
02:18:36,531 --> 02:18:40,660
<i>I sullied my master's
beloved Soryu with blood...</i>

1894
02:18:41,160 --> 02:18:43,955
<i>and I couldn't follow
my dad's last wishes!</i>

1895
02:18:46,916 --> 02:18:48,667
<i>That's right.</i>

1896
02:18:48,668 --> 02:18:51,462
<i>The one I wanted to kill...</i>

1897
02:18:56,759 --> 02:18:59,929
<i>Not good! Not good! Not good!
My sword flew off somewhere!</i>

1898
02:19:01,681 --> 02:19:03,933
<i>I can't stop him just by punching him!</i>

1899
02:19:14,485 --> 02:19:16,653
<i>Akaza's about to unleash
the Annihilation Type move</i>

1900
02:19:16,654 --> 02:19:18,573
<i>that he used on Mr. Rengoku!</i>

1901
02:19:21,909 --> 02:19:25,246
<i>I have to take Mr. Giyu with me
out of the attack range!</i>

1902
02:19:29,709 --> 02:19:31,919
Forget about me!

1903
02:19:37,466 --> 02:19:39,218
<i>I've got to kill them.</i>

1904
02:19:41,846 --> 02:19:43,723
<i>The weakling...</i>

1905
02:19:44,599 --> 02:19:46,475
<i>that I hate so much!</i>

1906
02:20:29,268 --> 02:20:31,812
<i>He attacked himself.</i>

1907
02:20:34,398 --> 02:20:37,109
<i>Why would he turn on himself like that?</i>

1908
02:20:37,568 --> 02:20:39,070
<i>Why?</i>

1909
02:20:42,198 --> 02:20:43,532
<i>For a second...</i>

1910
02:20:43,950 --> 02:20:46,661
<i>I could pick up the scent
of gratitude from Akaza.</i>

1911
02:20:47,787 --> 02:20:49,830
<i>Why did he smile?</i>

1912
02:20:54,126 --> 02:20:56,461
<i>That's enough! Stop it!</i>

1913
02:20:56,462 --> 02:20:58,965
<i>Don't regenerate!</i>

1914
02:20:59,632 --> 02:21:01,591
<i>The battle is over!</i>

1915
02:21:01,592 --> 02:21:03,844
<i>I lost!</i>

1916
02:21:05,429 --> 02:21:08,765
<i>I lost decisively in that moment!</i>

1917
02:21:08,766 --> 02:21:13,396
<i>That was a clean, splendid technique!</i>

1918
02:21:14,730 --> 02:21:16,856
<i>You anticipated
the enemy's movements to perfection,</i>

1919
02:21:16,857 --> 02:21:18,984
<i>pivoted at the last second...</i>

1920
02:21:18,985 --> 02:21:22,780
<i>and struck before the enemy had finished
unleashing his move!</i>

1921
02:21:23,489 --> 02:21:25,116
<i>It's over now.</i>

1922
02:21:26,117 --> 02:21:27,784
<i>I want to accept my fate...</i>

1923
02:21:27,785 --> 02:21:30,413
<i>and go to Hell.</i>

1924
02:21:33,499 --> 02:21:35,584
<i>Where does he want to go?</i>

1925
02:21:43,384 --> 02:21:45,011
<i>He stopped in his tracks.</i>

1926
02:21:47,888 --> 02:21:49,223
<i>Dad...</i>

1927
02:21:51,058 --> 02:21:52,935
<i>Are you all right now?</i>

1928
02:21:53,394 --> 02:21:55,938
<i>You're not in any pain?</i>

1929
02:21:56,564 --> 02:21:59,233
<i>I'm fine, Hakuji.</i>

1930
02:22:00,192 --> 02:22:02,069
<i>Thank you, Son.</i>

1931
02:22:08,409 --> 02:22:10,411
<i>Sorry, Dad.</i>

1932
02:22:10,786 --> 02:22:14,247
<i>Sorry I couldn't start over.</i>

1933
02:22:14,248 --> 02:22:16,000
<i>It didn't work out.</i>

1934
02:22:18,961 --> 02:22:20,796
<i>It doesn't matter.</i>

1935
02:22:21,630 --> 02:22:27,219
<i>No matter how you turn out,
you're my son and student.</i>

1936
02:22:27,595 --> 02:22:29,930
<i>We won't desert you even in death!</i>

1937
02:22:31,057 --> 02:22:34,810
<i>Though we can't take you
with us to Heaven.</i>

1938
02:22:36,979 --> 02:22:38,773
<i>Master...</i>

1939
02:22:41,192 --> 02:22:44,779
<i>Didn't you want to become stronger?</i>

1940
02:22:45,321 --> 02:22:48,615
<i>Is this it for you...</i>

1941
02:22:48,616 --> 02:22:50,534
<i>Akaza?</i>

1942
02:22:51,911 --> 02:22:53,661
<i>That's right.</i>

1943
02:22:53,662 --> 02:22:55,622
<i>I'm going to get stronger.</i>

1944
02:22:55,623 --> 02:22:57,917
<i>I want to become stronger!</i>

1945
02:22:58,584 --> 02:23:00,794
<i>So, what if I got beheaded?</i>

1946
02:23:00,795 --> 02:23:03,756
<i>Win? Lose? Who cares?</i>

1947
02:23:04,215 --> 02:23:06,550
<i>I'm going to kill 'em all!</i>

1948
02:23:07,468 --> 02:23:10,554
<i>I can still become stronger!</i>

1949
02:23:12,890 --> 02:23:16,560
<i>I have to keep my promise!</i>

1950
02:23:26,821 --> 02:23:28,697
<i>Mr. Hakuji...</i>

1951
02:23:29,365 --> 02:23:30,741
<i>Thank you.</i>

1952
02:23:31,450 --> 02:23:33,536
<i>That's enough.</i>

1953
02:23:37,790 --> 02:23:39,707
<i>That's enough now.</i>

1954
02:23:39,708 --> 02:23:41,292
<i>It's all right.</i>

1955
02:23:41,293 --> 02:23:43,003
<i>Akaza!</i>

1956
02:23:53,305 --> 02:23:55,682
<i>I'm sorry! I'm sorry!</i>

1957
02:23:55,683 --> 02:23:57,726
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't protect you!</i>

1958
02:23:58,060 --> 02:24:01,021
<i>I'm sorry I wasn't there
when it counted the most!</i>

1959
02:24:01,856 --> 02:24:04,649
<i>I couldn't keep a single promise I made!</i>

1960
02:24:04,650 --> 02:24:05,985
<i>Forgive me!</i>

1961
02:24:06,318 --> 02:24:08,988
<i>I'm begging you, please forgive me!</i>

1962
02:24:09,488 --> 02:24:11,574
<i>Forgive me!</i>

1963
02:24:15,453 --> 02:24:17,620
<i>I'm so glad...</i>

1964
02:24:17,621 --> 02:24:20,332
<i>that you remembered us.</i>

1965
02:24:21,333 --> 02:24:26,046
<i>I'm so glad that you're back
to being the Mr. Hakuji that I know!</i>

1966
02:24:34,597 --> 02:24:37,766
<i>Welcome home, Hakuji.</i>

1967
02:24:41,770 --> 02:24:43,522
<i>Hey, Hakuji!</i>

1968
02:24:43,856 --> 02:24:45,733
<i>Welcome home!</i>

1969
02:24:53,866 --> 02:24:55,201
<i>I'm home.</i>

1970
02:24:56,535 --> 02:24:58,370
<i>I'm back now.</i>

1971
02:25:01,790 --> 02:25:03,626
<i>Welcome home...</i>

1972
02:25:04,585 --> 02:25:06,003
<i>my darling!</i>

1973
02:25:10,299 --> 02:25:11,425
<i>Hey...</i>

1974
02:25:35,199 --> 02:25:36,825
<i>He vanished.</i>

1975
02:25:48,379 --> 02:25:51,173
It's... over.

1976
02:25:54,593 --> 02:25:55,844
Gotta hurry.

1977
02:25:56,720 --> 02:25:58,097
We've got to...

1978
02:25:58,472 --> 02:26:00,057
go to Ms. Tamayo...

1979
02:26:01,308 --> 02:26:02,893
next...

1980
02:26:10,359 --> 02:26:11,777
Tanjiro!

1981
02:26:24,707 --> 02:26:26,916
Tanjiro, Giyu...

1982
02:26:26,917 --> 02:26:29,545
have defeated Upper Three!

1983
02:26:29,837 --> 02:26:33,506
They are unable to stay conscious
due to exhaustion!

1984
02:26:33,507 --> 02:26:35,050
They've passed out!

1985
02:26:40,389 --> 02:26:42,724
Tanjiro, Giyu...

1986
02:26:42,725 --> 02:26:45,810
have defeated Upper Three!

1987
02:26:45,811 --> 02:26:47,646
Upper Three!

1988
02:26:54,361 --> 02:26:55,946
Akaza's...

1989
02:26:56,322 --> 02:26:58,866
presence is gone.

1990
02:27:01,285 --> 02:27:03,829
Who knew that he'd lose?

1991
02:27:06,915 --> 02:27:08,500
Akaza!

1992
02:27:09,835 --> 02:27:13,672
Weren't you going to defeat me?

1993
02:27:15,924 --> 02:27:20,220
Who knew that you'd willingly abandon...

1994
02:27:21,889 --> 02:27:25,267
the path you opened to greater heights?

1995
02:27:31,982 --> 02:27:35,361
How absurdly weak!

1996
02:27:42,326 --> 02:27:43,743
Could...

1997
02:27:43,744 --> 02:27:45,578
Lord Akaza...

1998
02:27:45,579 --> 02:27:48,791
possibly be d-dead?

1999
02:27:49,541 --> 02:27:54,380
I felt a weird presence for a moment,
but it was just my imagination, right?

2000
02:27:55,172 --> 02:27:56,714
Like Lord Akaza...

2001
02:27:56,715 --> 02:27:59,677
had turned into some other creature.

2002
02:28:02,471 --> 02:28:05,265
Well, now that he's dead, I have no clue!

2003
02:28:08,435 --> 02:28:10,144
Let's see.

2004
02:28:10,145 --> 02:28:11,730
Where was I?

2005
02:28:12,314 --> 02:28:14,024
Oh, right, I remember!

2006
02:28:14,733 --> 02:28:17,361
I'd asked you your name, right?

2007
02:28:30,249 --> 02:28:32,500
Tanjiro, Giyu...

2008
02:28:32,501 --> 02:28:34,628
have defeated Upper Three!

2009
02:28:35,629 --> 02:28:36,630
Upper Three!

2010
02:28:37,506 --> 02:28:38,798
Mr. Himejima!

2011
02:28:38,799 --> 02:28:39,883
Yes.

2012
02:28:40,259 --> 02:28:42,010
Good job, Tomioka!

2013
02:28:42,803 --> 02:28:44,596
Good job, Kamado!

2014
02:28:49,768 --> 02:28:53,355
That's amazing,
Mr. Tomioka, Tanjiro!

2015
02:28:53,814 --> 02:28:56,525
We're going to follow their lead.

2016
02:28:56,900 --> 02:28:57,901
Right!

2017
02:29:12,708 --> 02:29:14,710
Don't die, Agatsuma!

2018
02:29:20,215 --> 02:29:23,761
If you don't hurry it up, I'll poke you!
Listen up!

2019
02:29:24,303 --> 02:29:27,638
Show me where the strongest demon is!

2020
02:29:27,639 --> 02:29:29,558
Got that?

2021
02:29:29,850 --> 02:29:32,436
Comin' through!

2022
02:29:33,395 --> 02:29:34,896
This way! This way!

2023
02:29:34,897 --> 02:29:38,192
There's a powerful
guy over here!

2024
02:29:44,615 --> 02:29:46,492
Where's Big Brother?

2025
02:29:56,668 --> 02:29:58,544
Bring me
an Upper Rank!

2026
02:29:58,545 --> 02:29:59,712
An Upper Rank!

2027
02:29:59,713 --> 02:30:01,256
Hey!

2028
02:30:01,632 --> 02:30:04,051
Stop running
from me!

2029
02:30:12,267 --> 02:30:13,935
The passageway
leading north...

2030
02:30:13,936 --> 02:30:15,520
on the 88th level...

2031
02:30:15,521 --> 02:30:17,481
no sign of Muzan.

2032
02:30:18,398 --> 02:30:19,398
The 100th...

2033
02:30:19,399 --> 02:30:21,275
and 27th levels in
the southeast...

2034
02:30:21,276 --> 02:30:23,070
no sign of Muzan.

2035
02:30:24,196 --> 02:30:25,488
Where?

2036
02:30:25,489 --> 02:30:27,866
Where is he?
Where could he be?

2037
02:30:28,951 --> 02:30:31,118
No sign of Muzan...

2038
02:30:31,119 --> 02:30:33,622
on any of the levels
from 90 to 100, either.

2039
02:30:35,457 --> 02:30:37,625
Covering the entire
100th and 33rd levels.

2040
02:30:37,626 --> 02:30:40,337
No sign of Muzan.

2041
02:30:41,672 --> 02:30:46,385
Our crows'll find
you without fail!

2042
02:30:47,052 --> 02:30:49,930
We're going
over this castle...

2043
02:30:50,347 --> 02:30:52,306
with a fine-tooth
comb, and...

2044
02:30:52,307 --> 02:30:54,768
we'll track you down
wherever you go!

2045
02:30:58,397 --> 02:30:59,773
{\an8}FOUR

2046
02:31:09,366 --> 02:31:12,202
Multi-layered structures are
now moving to the northeast.

2047
02:31:12,494 --> 02:31:14,245
New structures
are moving...

2048
02:31:14,246 --> 02:31:16,164
vertically and
horizontally!

2049
02:31:16,665 --> 02:31:18,292
Folding over themselves!

2050
02:31:21,962 --> 02:31:23,672
- And becoming one!
- And becoming one!

2051
02:31:30,387 --> 02:31:32,222
Who would've thought...

2052
02:31:33,599 --> 02:31:34,683
No...

2053
02:31:35,017 --> 02:31:37,978
we don't have the option
to lose.

2054
02:31:38,645 --> 02:31:40,647
Crows, go on!

2055
02:31:41,148 --> 02:31:42,774
To where Muzan is!

2056
02:31:47,738 --> 02:31:50,198
Those eyesore
Demon Slayers!

2057
02:31:50,574 --> 02:31:54,578
You'll never be able
to reach me!

2058
02:31:54,995 --> 02:31:56,621
You may be
feeling smug...

2059
02:31:56,622 --> 02:31:58,707
about beheading
an Upper Rank...

2060
02:31:59,082 --> 02:32:00,958
but unless
you kill me...

2061
02:32:00,959 --> 02:32:03,086
it means nothing!

2062
02:32:06,882 --> 02:32:12,595
You're going to die meaninglessly
without ever seeing my face!

2063
02:32:12,596 --> 02:32:16,516
So fitting for you foolish,
meaningless lot!

2064
02:32:17,309 --> 02:32:18,768
When I'm done here...

2065
02:32:18,769 --> 02:32:22,522
I'm going to make you regret
that you were ever alive!

2066
02:32:23,857 --> 02:32:27,778
You're going to struggle, suffer
and writhe around in pain!

2067
02:32:28,111 --> 02:32:30,237
And for you Demon Slayers...

2068
02:32:30,238 --> 02:32:33,158
this will be your final night...

2069
02:32:33,450 --> 02:32:35,827
the day of your death!

2070
02:32:46,797 --> 02:32:48,674
Don't die!

2071
02:32:51,969 --> 02:32:54,179
Giyu!

2072
02:33:00,852 --> 02:33:05,190
Tanjiro, don't you die on us!

2073
